-- TopWebExpert page rewrites (2026-09-23 07:04)
SET NAMES utf8mb4;
UPDATE city_pages SET title='Mobile App Development', content='<p>Most app projects that fail do not fail in the code. They fail because nobody asked, early enough, whether the app solves a problem people will open their phone for. At TopWebExpert we build Android and iOS apps from our office on Sohna Road, Sector 49, and we spend the first conversation on that question before we talk about screens or budgets. This page explains how we approach mobile app development in Gurugram: what we build, how we decide on the technology, what a typical project looks like week by week, and when we tell a client not to build an app at all.</p>\n\n<h2>Start With the Job the App Has to Do</h2>\n<p>Every app we take on begins with a one-page statement of the job it does for a specific user. A delivery rider in Manesar needs to mark a drop-off with one thumb while standing next to a truck. A patient at a clinic on Golf Course Road needs to rebook an appointment without calling the front desk. A sales team in Udyog Vihar needs to log a site visit even when the basement parking has no signal. These are very different apps, and writing the job down first stops the project from turning into a list of features copied from a competitor.</p>\n<p>From that statement we agree on the smallest version worth releasing. Anything outside it goes into a later-release list, not into the first build.</p>\n\n<h2>Native, Cross-Platform or a Web App: How We Choose</h2>\n<p>We do not have a favourite framework we push on every client. The choice follows from what the app needs:</p>\n<ul class=\"check-list\">\n<li><strong>Flutter or React Native</strong> for most business apps that need to run on both Android and iOS from one codebase. This usually keeps build and maintenance cost lower.</li>\n<li><strong>Native Kotlin (Android) or Swift (iOS)</strong> when the app leans heavily on device hardware, such as Bluetooth scanners, background location or camera processing.</li>\n<li><strong>A progressive web app (PWA)</strong> when users will only open it occasionally and would not bother installing anything. It works in the browser and can be added to the home screen.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The backend is typically Node.js or Laravel with a MySQL or PostgreSQL database, hosted on AWS or a similar cloud provider, with Firebase used for push notifications and crash reporting.</p>\n\n<h2>Details That Matter for Indian Users</h2>\n<p>An app that works well on a flagship phone in our office can struggle in the hands of real users. We design and test for the conditions most Indian users actually have:</p>\n<ul class=\"check-list\">\n<li><strong>Low-end Android phones</strong> with limited RAM and storage, so we keep the app size small and avoid heavy animations.</li>\n<li><strong>Patchy mobile data</strong>, so key screens cache content and forms save drafts offline.</li>\n<li><strong>Payments through UPI</strong>, cards and wallets via gateways such as Razorpay, with clear handling of failed and pending transactions.</li>\n<li><strong>WhatsApp Business API</strong> for order updates and OTPs, where customers are more likely to read a WhatsApp message than an email.</li>\n<li><strong>Hindi and Hinglish</strong> interface text when the audience needs it, planned from the start rather than bolted on later.</li>\n<li><strong>DPDP Act 2023</strong> obligations: clear consent screens, collecting only the personal data you need, and a way for users to ask for deletion.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>A Typical Build, Week by Week</h2>\n<p>Timelines depend on scope, but a first release of a business app usually follows this pattern:</p>\n<ol class=\"steps\">\n<li><strong>Weeks 1–2: Discovery.</strong> A workshop at our Sector 49 office or yours, user flows, a feature list split into \"release 1\" and \"later\", and a fixed quote.</li>\n<li><strong>Weeks 3–4: Design.</strong> Wireframes, then clickable Figma screens you can try on your own phone before any code is written.</li>\n<li><strong>Weeks 5–12: Development.</strong> Two-week sprints, each ending with a test build you install through TestFlight or an Android test link.</li>\n<li><strong>Weeks 12–14: Testing and store submission.</strong> Device testing, fixes, store listings, privacy declarations and submission to Google Play and the App Store.</li>\n<li><strong>After launch:</strong> a stabilisation period for bug fixes, then an optional maintenance plan covering OS updates and new features.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Simple apps can be quicker. Apps with complex integrations, such as an ERP connection or a multi-vendor marketplace, take longer, and we say so in the quote.</p>\n\n<h2>What We Need From You</h2>\n<ul class=\"check-list\">\n<li>One decision-maker who can approve screens within a few days.</li>\n<li>Your brand assets, content and any existing API documentation.</li>\n<li>Your own Google Play Console and Apple Developer accounts, so the app is listed under your business name.</li>\n<li>Access to a few real users for feedback on the test builds.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>Who Owns the App and the Code</h2>\n<p>Once the project is paid for, you own the source code, designs and store listings. The code lives in a Git repository under your account, the apps are published under your developer accounts, and server credentials are handed over at the end. If you later move to an in-house team or another vendor, nothing is locked up with us.</p>\n\n<h2>How We Check Quality</h2>\n<p>Every build is tested on a mix of devices, including budget Android phones, not just emulators. We run code reviews on every change, automated tests on business logic such as pricing and payments, and crash monitoring from day one of the beta. Before store submission we go through Google and Apple review guidelines to avoid rejections that delay launch.</p>\n\n<h2>Mistakes We Help Clients Avoid</h2>\n<ul class=\"check-list\">\n<li>Building every feature for version one instead of releasing a focused app and learning from usage.</li>\n<li>Publishing under the agency\'s developer account, which makes switching vendors painful later.</li>\n<li>Ignoring the admin panel. Your team will use it daily, so it needs as much care as the customer app.</li>\n<li>Skipping a budget for maintenance. Android and iOS release updates every year, and apps need to keep up.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>When an App Is the Wrong Answer</h2>\n<p>We are not a good fit if you want an app mainly because competitors have one, if customers interact with you once or twice a year, or if you need a working product in two weeks. In those cases a fast, mobile-friendly website or a WhatsApp-based flow is often the smarter spend, and we will tell you that in the first meeting.</p>\n\n<h2>Questions Gurugram Businesses Ask Us</h2>\n<h3>How much does it cost to build an app?</h3>\n<p>Cost depends on the number of screens, the platforms, integrations such as payments or an ERP, and whether you need an admin panel. We do not quote from a rate card. After a free consultation and a short discovery, we give you a fixed quote tied to a written scope.</p>\n<h3>Can you take over an app another agency started?</h3>\n<p>Yes, provided we can get the source code and account access. We start with a code audit and tell you honestly whether to continue with the existing code or rebuild parts of it.</p>\n<h3>Will my app work on older Android phones?</h3>\n<p>We agree a minimum Android and iOS version at the start based on your users, and we test on lower-end devices before release.</p>\n<h3>Do we have to meet in person?</h3>\n<p>No, but many clients based in Cyber City, Golf Course Road or around Gurgaon\'s Sohna Road belt find a half-day workshop at our office the quickest way to settle scope. Everything after that can run on calls and shared test builds.</p>\n<h3>What happens after the app goes live?</h3>\n<p>We fix launch bugs as part of the project, then offer an optional monthly maintenance plan for OS updates, security patches and new features.</p>\n\n<p>If you are planning mobile app development in Gurugram, visit us at Tower B1, Spaze I-Tech Park, Sohna Road, Sector 49, or call +91 9050126213. <a href=\"/contact-us\">Book a free consultation</a> and we will help you work out whether an app is the right move and what the first release should include.</p>', meta_title='Mobile App Development in Gurugram | TopWebExpert', meta_description='Android and iOS apps built in Gurugram for Indian users: UPI payments, low-end phones, DPDP compliance. Clear phases, you own the code. Free consultation.', meta_keywords='mobile app development gurugram, app development company gurgaon, android app developers gurugram, flutter app development india, ios app development gurugram', updated_at=NOW(), tier=1 WHERE service_slug='app-development' AND location_id=(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE slug='gurgaon' LIMIT 1);
UPDATE city_pages SET title='Content Marketing', content='<p>Before most people contact a business, they have already read about the problem they want solved. A family comparing homes on Dwarka Expressway and Golf Course Extension Road reads about possession timelines and maintenance charges. A parent in Sector 56 reads about how a coaching institute runs its doubt sessions. A procurement lead at a GCC in Cyber City reads a vendor\'s guides before booking a demo. Content marketing is the work of answering those questions better than anyone else, so that your business is the one people trust when they are ready to buy. This is what our content team does at TopWebExpert.</p>\n\n<h2>What Content Marketing Is, and What It Is Not</h2>\n<p>It is a planned, steady body of useful material: articles, guides, videos, email newsletters and social posts built around the real questions of your customers. It is not publishing a blog post a day, rewriting competitors\' articles or stuffing a city name into every paragraph. Search engines now reward pages written from real experience and penalise mass-produced filler, so we write fewer, deeper pieces with input from the people in your business who know the subject.</p>\n\n<h2>Questions Your Buyers Ask Before They Call</h2>\n<p>We start by collecting the questions your sales team, receptionists and customer support hear every week. Some examples from typical Gurugram businesses:</p>\n<ul class=\"check-list\">\n<li><strong>Real estate:</strong> \"What is the difference between carpet area and super area?\" or \"What should I check in a builder-buyer agreement?\"</li>\n<li><strong>Hospitals and clinics:</strong> \"How long is recovery after a knee replacement?\" or \"Which tests should I do before surgery?\"</li>\n<li><strong>B2B SaaS and IT services:</strong> \"How do we move from spreadsheets to a CRM without losing data?\"</li>\n<li><strong>D2C brands:</strong> \"How do I choose the right size?\" or \"Is this product safe for sensitive skin?\"</li>\n<li><strong>Manufacturing and logistics around Manesar:</strong> \"What documents does a first-time exporter need?\"</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Each question becomes a potential piece of content, and we rank them by how often they come up, how close they are to a purchase decision and what already exists online.</p>\n\n<h2>The First 90 Days</h2>\n<ol class=\"steps\">\n<li><strong>Weeks 1–2: Audit and interviews.</strong> We review your existing website, social channels and analytics, and interview your founders, sales staff or doctors. The interviews can happen at our Sohna Road office in Sector 49, at your premises or over a call.</li>\n<li><strong>Weeks 3–4: Strategy and calendar.</strong> Keyword and question research, a list of priority topics, a content calendar for the quarter and an agreed tone of voice.</li>\n<li><strong>Weeks 5–12: Production.</strong> Writing, editing, design and publishing on an agreed schedule, alongside updates to existing pages that are close to ranking but underperforming.</li>\n<li><strong>Week 13: Review.</strong> A report on what was published, what is gaining traction and what we will change in the next quarter.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h2>Who Writes, and Who Checks</h2>\n<p>Every piece goes through a clear editorial chain: a writer drafts from an outline and your expert\'s input, an editor checks structure, facts and readability, and a subject expert on your side approves it before it goes live. Where AI tools help with research or outlines, a human writes and fact-checks the final text.</p>\n<p>Some industries need extra care. Medical content should be reviewed by a qualified doctor, and we name the reviewer on the page. Real estate project content must show the RERA registration number where a registered project is promoted. Advertising claims should follow ASCI guidelines. We flag these requirements up front rather than leaving you exposed.</p>\n\n<h2>Formats We Produce</h2>\n<ul class=\"tag-list\">\n<li>Long-form guides</li>\n<li>Blog articles</li>\n<li>Service and landing page copy</li>\n<li>Email newsletters</li>\n<li>LinkedIn posts and articles</li>\n<li>Short video scripts</li>\n<li>Case study write-ups from your own data</li>\n<li>Downloadable checklists</li>\n<li>Hindi and Hinglish social content</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Our working tools include Google Search Console, Google Analytics 4, Ahrefs or Semrush for research, Grammarly and plagiarism checkers for editing, Canva and Figma for visuals, and WordPress or your existing CMS for publishing.</p>\n\n<h2>How We Report Progress, Honestly</h2>\n<p>Content marketing is slow. New articles often take several months to rank, and we will not promise traffic or lead numbers up front. What we do report every month is what was published, which pages are gaining impressions and clicks in Search Console, which topics bring enquiries through your forms or WhatsApp, and what we plan to change as a result. You see the raw data, not a slide of vanity metrics.</p>\n\n<h2>Rights to the Content</h2>\n<p>Everything we write and design for you belongs to you once invoiced work is paid for, including drafts, images we create and the content calendar. Stock images and fonts are licensed properly, and every article is original. If you stop working with us, the content stays on your website and in your accounts.</p>\n\n<h2>What You Need to Provide</h2>\n<ul class=\"check-list\">\n<li>Time with at least one subject expert each month, even 30 minutes on a call.</li>\n<li>Access to your website CMS, Google Search Console and Analytics.</li>\n<li>Product details, pricing policies and any brand guidelines.</li>\n<li>One person who approves content within an agreed turnaround.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>Habits That Waste a Content Budget</h2>\n<ul class=\"check-list\">\n<li>Publishing many thin posts instead of a few thorough ones.</li>\n<li>Creating near-identical pages for every locality or city with only the name changed.</li>\n<li>Writing only about the company and never about the customer\'s problem.</li>\n<li>Never updating old articles that are close to ranking.</li>\n<li>Judging results after four weeks and stopping before the work has had time to work.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>When Content Marketing Will Not Help You Yet</h2>\n<p>If you need sales this month, paid ads or direct outreach will act faster. If your website is slow, broken on mobile or has no clear way to enquire, fix that first, or new content will not convert. And if no one in the business can spare time to share expertise, the content will stay generic, which is exactly what search engines and readers now ignore.</p>\n\n<h2>Content Marketing FAQs</h2>\n<h3>How long before we see results?</h3>\n<p>Expect early signs, such as rising impressions in Search Console, within a few months, and meaningful enquiries over a longer period. It depends on your competition, your site\'s history and how consistently content is published.</p>\n<h3>How is pricing decided?</h3>\n<p>It depends on the number and depth of pieces each month, the formats, research needs, design work and whether you need Hindi content. After a free consultation we send a fixed monthly or project quote.</p>\n<h3>Can you write about technical or medical subjects?</h3>\n<p>Yes, with your experts\' input. We interview them, draft from their answers and have them approve the final version.</p>\n<h3>Will you post on our social media too?</h3>\n<p>We can plan and create social posts from the same content and schedule them, or hand them to your in-house team.</p>\n<h3>Do we need a local agency for this?</h3>\n<p>Not necessarily, but being based in Gurgaon helps. We can visit your site, interview your team in person and understand local buyers first-hand.</p>\n\n<p>If you are considering content marketing in Gurugram, visit us at Tower B1, Spaze I-Tech Park, Sohna Road, Sector 49, or call +91 9050126213. <a href=\"/contact-us\">Book a free consultation</a> and bring the five questions your customers ask most often. We will show you how to turn them into content.</p>', meta_title='Content Marketing Services in Gurugram | TopWebExpert', meta_description='Content built on your customers\' real questions: guides, blogs, newsletters and Hindi social posts, reviewed by your experts. Honest monthly reporting.', meta_keywords='content marketing gurugram, content marketing agency gurgaon, content writing services gurugram, blog writing services india, seo content marketing gurugram', updated_at=NOW(), tier=1 WHERE service_slug='content-marketing' AND location_id=(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE slug='gurgaon' LIMIT 1);
UPDATE city_pages SET title='E-Commerce Website Development in Gurugram', content='<p>An online store in India succeeds or fails on details that have little to do with design: whether UPI payments go through smoothly, whether COD orders turn into returns, whether the GST invoice is correct, and whether the buyer can see that you deliver to their pincode. We build e-commerce websites from our office on Sohna Road for Gurugram D2C brands, retailers, distributors and manufacturers moving into online ordering. This page covers the decisions you will face, how the build works and what can go wrong.</p><h2>Start with how your orders actually work</h2><p>Before we talk about platforms or design, we ask questions about your operations. The answers shape the whole store:</p><ul class=\"check-list\"><li><strong>Who is buying?</strong> Retail customers (B2C), businesses ordering in bulk (B2B), or both. B2B buyers usually need GSTIN on invoices, quantity pricing and sometimes credit terms.</li><li><strong>How many products and variants?</strong> Twenty kurtas in five sizes is a very different catalogue from 3,000 auto parts with fitment data.</li><li><strong>Where is stock held?</strong> One warehouse, a few stores, or an existing billing or ERP system that needs to stay in sync.</li><li><strong>How much COD will you accept?</strong> Cash on delivery lifts conversions but brings returns-to-origin, so we plan rules around it.</li><li><strong>Who packs and ships?</strong> Your own team with a courier aggregator, or a fulfilment partner.</li></ul><h2>Platforms we build on</h2><ul class=\"tag-list\"><li>WooCommerce</li><li>Shopify</li><li>Custom PHP / Laravel</li></ul><p><strong>WooCommerce</strong> runs on WordPress and suits stores that want full control, content-heavy product pages or unusual pricing rules, with no platform subscription. You manage hosting, updates and security, or pay someone to. <strong>Shopify</strong> suits brands that want a managed platform and fast setup, and are comfortable with monthly subscription and app costs. <strong>A custom build</strong> makes sense only for requirements the platforms handle badly, such as a dealer portal with customer-specific price lists. We recommend the platform after the operations questions above, not before.</p><h2>Payments, GST and cash on delivery</h2><p>This is where Indian stores lose most orders, so we spend real time on it:</p><ul class=\"check-list\"><li><strong>Payment gateway set-up</strong> with Razorpay, PayU or Cashfree, covering UPI, cards, net banking and wallets. Gateways run their own KYC, so we prepare the policy pages they look for.</li><li><strong>GST-ready invoices</strong> with your GSTIN, HSN codes, correct CGST/SGST or IGST depending on the delivery state, and an optional GSTIN field at checkout for business buyers.</li><li><strong>COD rules</strong>: turn it off above a set order value or for certain pincodes, add a COD fee if you choose, and confirm COD orders by OTP or WhatsApp before dispatch to cut fake orders.</li><li><strong>Failed payment recovery</strong>: clear retry options and reminder messages when a UPI payment times out.</li><li><strong>Refunds</strong> processed from the admin panel through the gateway, so your team is not doing bank transfers by hand.</li></ul><h2>Shipping, pincodes and returns</h2><p>We connect the store to a shipping aggregator such as Shiprocket, or directly to a courier like Delhivery, so that shipping labels and AWB numbers are created from the order screen. Buyers can check delivery availability and an estimated date by pincode on the product page, and receive tracking updates by email, SMS or WhatsApp. We also set up return and exchange requests so they reach your team as structured tickets rather than scattered messages.</p><h2>The build, stage by stage</h2><p>A store with a clean product sheet of up to a few hundred products typically takes <strong>6 to 10 weeks</strong>. Larger catalogues, ERP sync or B2B features add time.</p><ol class=\"steps\"><li><strong>Operations workshop</strong> (week 1): the questions above, plus shipping zones, taxes and policies.</li><li><strong>Design</strong> (weeks 2 to 3): home, category, product, cart and checkout pages designed mobile-first, because most buyers will shop on a phone.</li><li><strong>Development and integrations</strong> (weeks 3 to 7): store set-up, gateway, shipping, invoices, WhatsApp and email notifications.</li><li><strong>Catalogue import</strong> (overlaps with development): products loaded from your spreadsheet, images optimised, categories and filters set.</li><li><strong>Test orders and launch</strong> (final 1 to 2 weeks): real transactions on every payment method, then go-live and close monitoring of the first orders.</li></ol><h2>What you need to prepare</h2><ul class=\"check-list\"><li>A product spreadsheet: name, SKU, price, MRP, variants, weight, dimensions, HSN code and a short description for each item.</li><li>Product photos on a plain background, with consistent size and lighting across the range.</li><li>Business PAN, GST registration and a current account for gateway KYC.</li><li>Your shipping, returns, refund and cancellation policies, which we can help you write in plain language.</li><li>Decisions on COD limits, free-shipping thresholds and discount rules.</li></ul><h2>How we check the store before launch</h2><ul class=\"check-list\"><li>Real test orders on UPI, cards, net banking and COD, including a failed payment and a full refund.</li><li>Invoices checked for intra-state and inter-state orders.</li><li>Core Web Vitals and PageSpeed tested on category and product pages, which carry the most images.</li><li>Card data never touches your server; payments are handled on the gateway\'s side. Admin accounts get strong passwords and two-factor login where the platform supports it.</li><li>Automated backups of the product and order database, with a tested restore.</li></ul><h2>Mistakes that quietly cost sales</h2><p>The ones we see most: forcing account creation before checkout, hiding shipping charges until the last step, no pincode check so buyers in outer sectors are unsure you deliver, unlimited COD with no confirmation step, and product pages with one blurry photo and no size or material details.</p><h2>When you should not build your own store yet</h2><p>If you sell only a handful of products and have no budget for ads or content, your own store will get little traffic at first. A marketplace such as Amazon or Flipkart, or a WhatsApp Business catalogue, may be a better first step. We will say so if that is the case. An own store makes sense once you want your own customer data, repeat orders and margins free of marketplace commissions.</p><h2>What affects the quote</h2><p>Cost depends on the platform, the number of products and variants, custom design versus a customised theme, integrations (ERP, billing software, CRM), B2B features and whether we handle product data entry and photography coordination. You get a fixed quote after a free consultation, with ongoing costs such as platform, app and gateway fees listed separately so there are no surprises.</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>Should I sell on Amazon instead of building my own store?</h3><p>Many brands do both. Marketplaces bring ready traffic but keep the customer relationship and take a commission. Your own store costs more to drive traffic to but lets you build repeat buyers. We can help you plan the order in which to do them.</p><h3>Can I offer COD only in some areas?</h3><p>Yes. COD can be limited by pincode, order value or product, and we can add an OTP or WhatsApp confirmation for COD orders before they are shipped.</p><h3>Will the store produce GST invoices automatically?</h3><p>Yes. Invoices are generated with your GSTIN, HSN codes and the right tax split for the delivery state. Your accountant should review the set-up once before launch.</p><h3>Who owns the customer and order data?</h3><p>You do. The store, gateway and shipping accounts are all opened in your company\'s name, and you can export customers and orders at any time.</p><h3>Can you connect the store to our billing software?</h3><p>Often, yes, depending on whether the software offers an API or import tools. We check this in the consultation before promising anything.</p><p>If you are planning an online store in Gurugram, or rethinking one you built earlier in the Gurgaon days, visit us at Tower B1, Spaze I-Tech Park, Sohna Road, Sector 49, or <a href=\"/contact-us\">book a free consultation</a>. Bring a sample of your product list and we will walk you through the platform choice and a realistic timeline.</p>', meta_title='E-Commerce Website Development Gurugram | TopWebExpert', meta_description='Online stores built for Indian buyers: Razorpay, PayU or Cashfree with UPI, GST invoices, COD rules and Shiprocket shipping. Free consultation in Gurugram.', meta_keywords='ecommerce website development gurugram, ecommerce website development company in gurgaon, woocommerce store development gurugram, online store development gurgaon, d2c website development gurugram', updated_at=NOW(), tier=1 WHERE service_slug='ecommerce-website-development-company' AND location_id=(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE slug='gurgaon' LIMIT 1);
UPDATE city_pages SET title='Facebook Ads Management in Gurugram', content='<p>Google Ads catches people who are already searching. Facebook and Instagram ads work differently: they put your offer in front of people who were not looking for it yet, based on where they live, their interests and how they behave on Meta\'s apps. That makes them useful for a new cafe on Golf Course Extension Road, a D2C brand launching a product, a coaching institute opening admissions or a real estate project on Dwarka Expressway. It also makes them easy to waste money on, because the platform will happily deliver cheap clicks and cheap leads that never convert.</p>\n\n<p>This page covers how we plan and manage Meta ads (Facebook and Instagram) for Gurugram businesses, and the decisions that matter most.</p>\n\n<h2>The Three Decisions That Shape Every Campaign</h2>\n\n<h3>1. Where the lead goes</h3>\n<p>You have three main options, and the right one depends on how your sales team works:</p>\n<ul class=\"check-list\">\n<li><strong>Instant forms inside Facebook:</strong> quick for the user and usually low cost per lead, but quality can be weak because people submit with one tap. We add qualifying questions or a review step to raise quality.</li>\n<li><strong>Click-to-WhatsApp ads:</strong> the ad opens a WhatsApp chat with your business. In Gurugram this often suits clinics, salons, home services, restaurants and coaching, where customers are used to asking questions on WhatsApp first. It needs someone to reply quickly.</li>\n<li><strong>Website landing page:</strong> slower for the user but gives you better control and more data. Suits e-commerce and high-value enquiries.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>2. Who sees the ads</h3>\n<p>We usually target by location (a radius around your premises or selected areas of Gurugram and nearby NCR), age where relevant, and a few broad interests, then let Meta\'s delivery system find responsive people. Custom audiences built from your website visitors, video viewers, Instagram engagers and customer lists (uploaded securely and hashed) are used for remarketing and lookalikes.</p>\n\n<h3>3. What the ad actually says and shows</h3>\n<p>On Meta, creative does most of the targeting work. A clear short video of your actual clinic, food, classroom or site visit usually does better than a polished stock image. We plan creative in sets so we can test different hooks, formats (Reels, Stories, feed) and offers.</p>\n\n<h2>Our Setup Process</h2>\n\n<ol class=\"steps\">\n<li><strong>Week 1: Accounts and tracking.</strong> We check or set up Meta Business Manager (Business Portfolio) under your ownership, connect your Facebook Page, Instagram account and WhatsApp Business number, install the Meta Pixel and, where your website allows, the Conversions API for more reliable tracking.</li>\n<li><strong>Week 1-2: Offer and creative plan.</strong> We agree on the offer, write ad copy in English, Hindi or Hinglish depending on your audience, and brief you on the photos and videos we need.</li>\n<li><strong>Week 2: Launch.</strong> A small number of campaigns go live with separate ad sets for testing, and lead notifications are routed to your team by email, sheet or CRM.</li>\n<li><strong>Weeks 3-6: Test and cut.</strong> We pause weak creative, move budget to what produces qualified leads and refresh ads before the audience gets tired of them.</li>\n<li><strong>Monthly: Review.</strong> We look at lead quality with your team, not just lead count, and plan the next round of creative.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h2>What You Will Need to Provide</h2>\n\n<ul class=\"check-list\">\n<li>Admin access to your Facebook Page and Instagram account, and a Business Portfolio in your company\'s name</li>\n<li>Your own payment method on the ad account</li>\n<li>Raw photos and phone videos of your product, premises, team or project; we can guide you on shooting them</li>\n<li>A person who responds to leads and WhatsApp messages within minutes during working hours</li>\n<li>Weekly feedback on which leads were genuine</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>How Results Are Measured</h2>\n\n<p>Meta\'s own dashboard reports a lot of numbers, and several of them flatter the ads. We focus on the ones that connect to revenue:</p>\n\n<ul class=\"tag-list\">\n<li>Cost per qualified lead</li>\n<li>Lead-to-visit or lead-to-sale rate</li>\n<li>Messaging conversations started</li>\n<li>Purchases and return on ad spend (e-commerce)</li>\n<li>Frequency and creative fatigue</li>\n<li>GA4 sessions and conversions from paid social</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>For businesses selling offline, the most useful measure is your own lead sheet marked with outcomes. When possible, we send those outcomes back to Meta through the Conversions API so the platform learns which leads were real.</p>\n\n<h2>Where Gurugram Businesses Go Wrong With Meta Ads</h2>\n\n<ul class=\"check-list\">\n<li><strong>Boosting posts from the Page:</strong> the Boost button offers little control over objective, placement or tracking. It is fine for a quick announcement, not for lead generation.</li>\n<li><strong>Chasing the lowest cost per lead:</strong> a form with no questions will produce cheap leads, many of whom do not remember filling it. Real estate channel partners know this problem well.</li>\n<li><strong>Using the same creative for months:</strong> performance drops as the same people see the same ad repeatedly.</li>\n<li><strong>Ad account owned by a freelancer:</strong> if the relationship ends, you lose the Pixel data, audiences and history.</li>\n<li><strong>Slow follow-up:</strong> a lead called back the next day has often already spoken to two competitors.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>When Meta Ads Are Not the Right Channel</h2>\n\n<p>Facebook and Instagram ads are a poor fit for urgent-need services where people search at the moment of need, such as emergency plumbing or towing, where Google is stronger. They also struggle for niche B2B offers aimed at a few specific decision-makers, such as industrial suppliers in the Manesar belt, where LinkedIn or direct outreach often works better. And if you cannot produce any photos or videos of your own, results tend to be weak.</p>\n\n<h2>Facebook Ads FAQs</h2>\n\n<h3>Should we run ads on Facebook, Instagram or both?</h3>\n<p>Usually both, from the same campaign. Meta decides placement based on where your audience responds. For younger audiences in Gurugram, most delivery often ends up on Instagram Reels and Stories, but we let the data decide rather than assume.</p>\n\n<h3>Our leads never pick up the phone. What can we do?</h3>\n<p>Add qualifying questions to the form, use a higher-intent form type, call within minutes, and send a WhatsApp message immediately after submission. We also check if the ad promised something the form does not deliver.</p>\n\n<h3>Do you create the videos?</h3>\n<p>We write scripts, plan shots and edit the footage you record, and we can arrange a shoot at your premises for an added cost. Simple phone videos shot well often outperform expensive productions.</p>\n\n<h3>What will it cost?</h3>\n<p>Ad spend is paid directly to Meta and depends on how many people you want to reach and how competitive your audience is. Our management fee depends on campaign count and creative volume. We share a fixed quote after a free consultation.</p>\n\n<h3>Are there restrictions for property or finance ads?</h3>\n<p>Meta applies special rules to some categories, such as financial products and, in certain countries, housing, and may limit targeting options. We check the current policy for your category before launch so ads are not rejected.</p>\n\n<p>If you want a second opinion on your current Meta ads or a plan for a launch, <a href=\"/contact-us\">book a free consultation</a>. Meet us at Tower B1, Spaze I-Tech Park on Sohna Road, Sector 49, or call +91 9050126213 and email info@topwebexpert.com. Businesses across Gurgaon and the wider NCR are welcome to meet online if that is easier.</p>', meta_title='Facebook Ads Management in Gurugram | TopWebExpert', meta_description='Facebook and Instagram ads for Gurugram businesses: lead forms vs WhatsApp ads, Pixel and Conversions API tracking, creative testing and lead quality.', meta_keywords='facebook ads agency gurugram, facebook marketing gurgaon, instagram ads gurugram, meta ads management, click to whatsapp ads', updated_at=NOW(), tier=1 WHERE service_slug='facebook-marketing' AND location_id=(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE slug='gurgaon' LIMIT 1);
UPDATE city_pages SET title='Google Ads Management in Gurugram', content='<p>Google Ads can bring a Gurugram business enquiries on the same day a campaign goes live. It can also spend a month\'s budget on clicks from students, job seekers and people in the wrong city. The difference is almost always in the setup: what is tracked, which searches you pay for, where the ads show and what happens after the click.</p>\n\n<p>We manage Google Ads for businesses from our office on Sohna Road in Sector 49. Here is how we run accounts and what you should expect from any agency handling your ad spend.</p>\n\n<h2>Start With Tracking, Not Keywords</h2>\n\n<p>Before a single keyword is added, we make sure every valuable action is measured. Without this, Google\'s automated bidding optimizes for clicks instead of customers, and nobody can tell which campaign is working.</p>\n\n<ul class=\"check-list\">\n<li><strong>Form submissions</strong> tracked through Google Ads conversion tracking and Google Tag Manager, firing only on a real thank-you page or confirmed submit</li>\n<li><strong>Phone calls</strong> from ads and from the website, with a minimum call length so misdials do not count as leads</li>\n<li><strong>WhatsApp clicks</strong>, since many Gurugram customers prefer to message rather than call or fill a form</li>\n<li><strong>GA4 linked</strong> to Google Ads so you can see how ad visitors behave on the site</li>\n<li><strong>Offline conversion import</strong> (where your CRM or lead sheet allows it) so Google learns which leads turned into site visits, admissions or sales</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>The last point matters for real estate, education and healthcare, where many form fills never pick up the phone. Feeding back which leads were genuine helps the bidding system find more people like them.</p>\n\n<h2>How We Build a Campaign</h2>\n\n<ol class=\"steps\">\n<li><strong>Search intent research:</strong> we list the searches a real buyer types, from \"physiotherapy clinic near me\" to \"3 BHK Dwarka Expressway ready to move\", and separate them from research or job-hunting searches. Many people still type \"Gurgaon\" instead of Gurugram, so both spellings go into the keyword list.</li>\n<li><strong>Negative keywords:</strong> we block terms like \"jobs\", \"salary\", \"course\", \"free\", \"PDF\" and competitor-irrelevant searches from day one, then keep adding from the search terms report.</li>\n<li><strong>Location targeting:</strong> we target the areas you actually serve, by radius around your location or by selected pincodes and areas, and set it to people located in those areas rather than people merely interested in them.</li>\n<li><strong>Ad copy and assets:</strong> ads that mention specifics such as the locality, timings, parking, or a same-day slot, with sitelinks, callouts and call assets.</li>\n<li><strong>Landing page:</strong> a focused page for each offer, loading fast on mobile, with a short form, a call button and a WhatsApp button. Sending ad traffic to a busy homepage wastes money.</li>\n<li><strong>Launch and learning:</strong> we start with controlled bids, watch search terms daily for the first two weeks, and move to automated bidding only once enough conversions are recorded.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<p>A typical setup, from access to live campaigns, takes one to two weeks. The first four to six weeks after launch are a learning period in which we cut waste and refine targeting.</p>\n\n<h2>Campaign Types We Use, and When</h2>\n\n<ul class=\"tag-list\">\n<li>Search campaigns</li>\n<li>Performance Max</li>\n<li>Call ads</li>\n<li>YouTube video campaigns</li>\n<li>Display remarketing</li>\n<li>Demand Gen</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>For most local service businesses, Search campaigns do the heavy lifting because they catch people who are ready to act. Performance Max can work well for businesses with good conversion data and strong creative, but it needs tight tracking and exclusions or it tends to drift towards cheap, low-quality placements. YouTube and Demand Gen help with launches and real estate projects where people need to see the product before enquiring.</p>\n\n<h2>What Drives Your Monthly Cost</h2>\n\n<p>There are two separate costs: the ad spend you pay Google directly, and our management fee. Ad spend depends on how competitive your searches are (legal, real estate and some healthcare terms cost much more per click than, say, a cafe), how many areas you target and how many enquiries you want. Our fee depends on the number of campaigns, landing pages and tracking work involved. After a free account audit or discovery call, we give a fixed quote and a recommended starting budget with reasoning, not a figure picked to look attractive.</p>\n\n<h2>Signs Your Current Account Is Leaking Money</h2>\n\n<ul class=\"check-list\">\n<li>Broad match keywords with no negative keyword list</li>\n<li>Location set to \"presence or interest\", showing ads to people outside Gurugram</li>\n<li>Conversions counting page views or button clicks instead of real enquiries</li>\n<li>All keywords in one ad group with one generic ad</li>\n<li>Auto-applied recommendations switched on without anyone reviewing them</li>\n<li>No one has looked at the search terms report in weeks</li>\n<li>The agency owns the ad account, not you</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>The last point is important. The Google Ads account should be created under your business and you should keep admin access. We work as managers on your account, so the data and history stay with you if you ever change agencies.</p>\n\n<h2>What You Need to Give Us</h2>\n\n<ul class=\"check-list\">\n<li>Admin access to your Google Ads account, or a billing profile so we can create one in your name</li>\n<li>Access to the website or a developer who can add tracking</li>\n<li>Your service areas, working hours and how quickly the team can respond to leads</li>\n<li>Honest feedback on lead quality every week, at least in the first month</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>Who Should Not Run Google Ads Yet</h2>\n\n<p>Paid search is hard to make profitable if nobody answers the phone during ad hours, if the website does not work on mobile, or if the average sale is too small to cover the cost of a click and follow-up. It is also a weak fit for products nobody is searching for yet; a new category often needs awareness through social media first.</p>\n\n<h2>Google Ads Questions From Business Owners</h2>\n\n<h3>How soon will we get leads?</h3>\n<p>Search ads can bring enquiries within the first few days of going live. Lead quality and cost per lead usually improve over the first four to six weeks as we add negatives and the bidding system learns.</p>\n\n<h3>Can we show ads only in specific sectors?</h3>\n<p>Yes, within limits. Google lets us target a radius around a point or specific postal areas. It cannot target individual sectors perfectly, but a clinic on Sohna Road can target nearby areas rather than the whole of Gurugram or Delhi NCR.</p>\n\n<h3>Why do we get so many irrelevant leads?</h3>\n<p>Usually because of broad keywords, missing negatives, weak form questions or Performance Max running without exclusions. A short account audit normally shows the cause.</p>\n\n<h3>Who pays Google?</h3>\n<p>You do, directly, using your own card or invoice billing. Our management fee is billed separately, so you always see exactly what went to Google.</p>\n\n<h3>Do we need a new website?</h3>\n<p>Not always. Often one or two dedicated landing pages are enough. We will tell you after reviewing your site.</p>\n\n<p>If you are running ads and unsure where the money goes, or planning to start, <a href=\"/contact-us\">book a free Google Ads audit or consultation</a>. Our team works from Spaze I-Tech Park on Sohna Road, Sector 49, which is easy to reach from most of south Gurugram. Call +91 9050126213 or email info@topwebexpert.com.</p>', meta_title='Google Ads Management in Gurugram | TopWebExpert', meta_description='Google Ads for Gurugram businesses: conversion tracking first, tight location targeting, negative keywords and landing pages. Free account audit and quote.', meta_keywords='google ads agency gurugram, google ads management gurgaon, ppc company gurugram, google adwords management, ppc services', updated_at=NOW(), tier=1 WHERE service_slug='google-marketing' AND location_id=(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE slug='gurgaon' LIMIT 1);
UPDATE city_pages SET title='Google Business Profile Optimization in Gurugram', content='<p>For a restaurant near Cyber Hub, a diagnostic lab in Sector 56 or a car workshop on the Manesar side, the Google Business Profile is often the first thing a customer sees, before the website and sometimes instead of it. It shows your hours, photos, reviews, phone number and a button for directions. When it is incomplete, wrong or suspended, you lose calls you never knew were coming.</p>\n\n<p>Our Google Business Profile optimization service is a focused piece of work: we audit the profile, fix what is broken, fill in what is missing and hand you a simple routine to keep it active. We are based on Sohna Road in Sector 49, and we have spent 7+ years working on search and marketing for 150+ clients.</p>\n\n<h2>Is Your Profile Costing You Customers? A Quick Self-Check</h2>\n\n<p>Open your profile on your phone and look at it the way a new customer would. If any of these are true, there is work to do:</p>\n\n<ul class=\"check-list\">\n<li>The primary category is generic (for example \"Clinic\" when you are a physiotherapy centre)</li>\n<li>Opening hours are missing, or holiday hours were never updated for Diwali or other closures</li>\n<li>Photos are few, blurry, or were uploaded by customers only</li>\n<li>Recent reviews have no reply from the business</li>\n<li>The phone number goes to someone who has left, or to a landline nobody answers</li>\n<li>The pin on the map sits in the wrong tower of your business park or on the wrong side of the road</li>\n<li>There are two listings for the same business, often one created by a former employee</li>\n<li>The website link goes to the homepage instead of the relevant location page</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>Pin placement is a real problem in Gurugram. In large complexes such as the towers along Golf Course Road or the business parks on Sohna Road, a pin placed a few hundred metres off can send customers to the wrong gate. Another frequent question: many people still search \"Gurgaon\" rather than Gurugram. Google treats the two names as the same place, so there is no need to add either one to your business name.</p>\n\n<h2>The Optimization Work, Item by Item</h2>\n\n<h3>Categories and services</h3>\n<p>We choose the most accurate primary category and relevant secondary categories, then list your services with plain descriptions. Category choice has a strong effect on which searches you appear for.</p>\n\n<h3>Business information</h3>\n<p>Name exactly as on your signage (no added keywords), correct address or service area, phone, website link with tracking parameters, hours, holiday hours, and attributes such as wheelchair access or parking where they apply.</p>\n\n<h3>Photos and videos</h3>\n<p>We brief you on what to shoot: exterior with signage so people recognise it from the road, entrance and reception, team, work in progress and finished work. For restaurants, the menu and dishes; for clinics, the waiting area and equipment.</p>\n\n<h3>Description and posts</h3>\n<p>A clear business description written for customers, and a calendar of posts for offers, updates and events. Posts do not directly boost rankings much, but they show searchers the business is active.</p>\n\n<h3>Reviews</h3>\n<p>We set up a review request process using your profile\'s short link and a QR code, write reply templates for common situations, and advise on handling negative or fake reviews through Google\'s reporting process.</p>\n\n<h3>Duplicates and ownership</h3>\n<p>We help remove duplicate listings, recover access when a profile is owned by an old agency or former staff member, and guide you through verification, which Google now often handles through a short video of your premises and signage.</p>\n\n<h2>Timeline</h2>\n\n<ol class=\"steps\">\n<li><strong>Week 1:</strong> Access, audit and a list of issues ranked by impact.</li>\n<li><strong>Week 2:</strong> Category, information, pin and description fixes; photo brief sent to you.</li>\n<li><strong>Weeks 2-4:</strong> Photos uploaded, services listed, review process launched, duplicates reported.</li>\n<li><strong>Ongoing (optional):</strong> monthly posting, review reply support and a performance report.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<p>Some fixes depend on Google. Duplicate removal, ownership disputes and reinstatement after a suspension can take anywhere from days to several weeks, and we will tell you when a step is out of our hands.</p>\n\n<h2>What We Need From You</h2>\n\n<ul class=\"check-list\">\n<li>Access to the Google account that owns the profile, or manager access</li>\n<li>A photo of your signage and, for verification, the ability to record a short video at your premises</li>\n<li>A business document with the registered name and address if Google asks for proof</li>\n<li>Current photos, or time for a quick photo walk-through</li>\n<li>One person who will reply to reviews, or approval for us to reply on your behalf</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>How We Measure Whether It Worked</h2>\n\n<p>Google\'s profile performance data (what used to be called GBP Insights) shows searches that found you, calls, direction requests, website clicks and bookings where available. We record these before we start and compare month by month. We also add UTM tags to the website link so visits from the profile show up separately in GA4, and track calls and WhatsApp clicks from that traffic.</p>\n\n<ul class=\"tag-list\">\n<li>Calls from profile</li>\n<li>Direction requests</li>\n<li>Website clicks</li>\n<li>Search queries used</li>\n<li>Review count and rating</li>\n<li>Map-pack position by area</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>Who Does Not Need This</h2>\n\n<p>If your business has no physical location and no defined local service area, such as an online-only store, you are not eligible for a profile in the normal way and this service will not help. And if your profile is already complete, verified, with steady reviews and replies, you may only need occasional check-ins rather than a full project.</p>\n\n<h2>Google Business Profile FAQs</h2>\n\n<h3>Our profile got suspended after we changed the name. What now?</h3>\n<p>First, revert anything that breaks the guidelines, such as keywords in the name. Then submit a reinstatement request with supporting evidence like signage photos and registration documents. We prepare the evidence and submit the appeal with you.</p>\n\n<h3>We work from a flat in a residential society. Can we still have a profile?</h3>\n<p>Yes, as a service-area business, if you meet customers at their location. You hide your address and list the areas you serve. You should not show a home address as a storefront if customers do not visit.</p>\n\n<h3>Can you remove a bad review?</h3>\n<p>Only Google can remove reviews, and only if they break its policies, such as spam, conflicts of interest or offensive content. We help you flag those. For genuine complaints, a calm, factual reply often does more good than removal.</p>\n\n<h3>What does this cost?</h3>\n<p>It depends on the number of locations, whether there are ownership or suspension issues, and whether you want ongoing management. We quote a fixed price after a free profile audit.</p>\n\n<h3>Is this the same as local SEO?</h3>\n<p>It is one part of it. Local SEO also covers your website, directory listings and local links. Many businesses start with the profile because it gives the quickest visible improvement.</p>\n\n<p>Want someone to look over your listing? <a href=\"/contact-us\">Request a free profile audit</a>, or drop in at our office in Tower B1, Spaze I-Tech Park, Sohna Road, Sector 49. You can also call +91 9050126213 or email info@topwebexpert.com.</p>', meta_title='Google Business Profile Gurugram | TopWebExpert', meta_description='Fix and optimize your Google Business Profile in Gurugram: categories, map pin, photos, reviews, duplicates and suspensions, tracked with performance data.', meta_keywords='google business profile optimization, google my business gurugram, gmb optimization gurgaon, google listing suspended, google maps listing', updated_at=NOW(), tier=1 WHERE service_slug='google-my-business' AND location_id=(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE slug='gurgaon' LIMIT 1);
UPDATE city_pages SET title='Lead Generation Services', content='<p>\"We are getting leads, but they don\'t convert.\" It is one of the most common complaints from business owners, and Gurugram is no exception. A B2B supplier in Udyog Vihar may get enquiries from students and job seekers. A clinic on Golf Course Road may get form fills from people who never pick up the phone. An IT services firm in Cyber City may get plenty of cheap leads from ads, yet close almost none of them.</p>\n<p>The cause is usually the same. Somebody was asked to produce leads, so they optimised for the number of forms submitted. Our lead generation services in Gurugram start from the other end: what does a lead worth calling look like for your business, and what has to happen between the ad click and the sales call for that person to become a customer?</p>\n\n<h2>First, we agree what a \"lead\" means</h2>\n<p>Before any campaign is built, we sit down with you and whoever handles sales, and write a one-page definition. It covers:</p>\n<ul class=\"check-list\">\n<li><strong>Who qualifies:</strong> location, company size or household profile, budget range, and timeline.</li>\n<li><strong>Who doesn\'t:</strong> the enquiries you want filtered out, such as job applications, vendors pitching to you, or requests for services you don\'t offer.</li>\n<li><strong>What a sale is worth</strong> to you, roughly, so we know how much you can sensibly pay per qualified lead.</li>\n<li><strong>What happens next:</strong> who calls, how quickly, and how the outcome is recorded.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>This takes about an hour and it changes everything that follows. Campaign targeting, form questions and reports are all built around it.</p>\n\n<h2>Picking channels by how your buyers decide</h2>\n<h3>B2B and high-value services</h3>\n<p>Buyers research, compare and involve colleagues. Google Search campaigns on problem and service searches, LinkedIn campaigns aimed at job titles and industries, and a website with proper service pages and detailed content usually work well. Lead volume is lower; each lead is worth more. Long forms are acceptable here because they filter out casual enquiries.</p>\n<h3>Local consumer services</h3>\n<p>Clinics, salons, coaching centres, interior designers and home services depend on people nearby searching when they need something. A well-maintained Google Business Profile, local search campaigns targeted to specific sectors and localities, and click-to-call or click-to-WhatsApp ads fit this pattern. Speed of response matters more than anything else.</p>\n<h3>Considered consumer purchases</h3>\n<p>Education, property, cars and similar decisions take weeks. Meta and Google lead forms help build a pipeline, but follow-up by WhatsApp, SMS and email over several weeks does most of the converting.</p>\n\n<h2>What we build</h2>\n<ol class=\"steps\">\n<li><strong>Tracking.</strong> Google Analytics 4, Google Tag Manager, ad platform conversion tags and call tracking are set up so every lead can be traced to its source. Without this, no one can tell which spend is working.</li>\n<li><strong>Landing pages.</strong> One page per offer, loading quickly on mobile, with a form that asks the questions from your lead definition. Sending ad traffic to a general homepage wastes money.</li>\n<li><strong>Campaigns.</strong> Search, social or LinkedIn campaigns, depending on the channel plan above, with negative keywords and audience exclusions to keep out the people you don\'t want.</li>\n<li><strong>Lead forms with filters.</strong> For Meta and Google lead forms, we add qualifying questions and, where it helps, use the higher-intent form option that asks people to review their details before submitting.</li>\n<li><strong>Instant routing.</strong> Leads go straight to your CRM, or to a shared sheet and an email or WhatsApp alert if you don\'t use a CRM yet, with an automatic acknowledgement to the enquirer.</li>\n<li><strong>Feedback loop.</strong> Your team marks each lead\'s outcome. We feed qualified leads and sales back into the ad platforms where possible, so their algorithms learn to find more people like your real customers.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h2>The first 90 days</h2>\n<p><strong>Weeks 1–3:</strong> lead definition, tracking audit and setup, landing pages, and campaign build. <strong>Weeks 4–8:</strong> campaigns go live on a controlled budget. We check search terms and lead quality every few days, cut what brings junk and shift budget to what brings qualified enquiries. <strong>Weeks 9–12:</strong> with a few weeks of sales outcomes recorded, we can see real cost per qualified lead and cost per sale by channel, and decide with you whether to scale, change or stop each channel.</p>\n<p>We are honest about the early weeks. The first month is partly spent learning, and results rarely peak straight away.</p>\n\n<h2>Numbers we report</h2>\n<ul class=\"tag-list\">\n<li>Total leads</li>\n<li>Qualified lead rate</li>\n<li>Cost per lead</li>\n<li>Cost per qualified lead</li>\n<li>Response time</li>\n<li>Lead-to-meeting rate</li>\n<li>Cost per sale</li>\n</ul>\n<p>We treat cost per lead on its own as a misleading figure. A channel with double the cost per lead can be the cheaper one if its leads close three times as often.</p>\n\n<h2>Why leads fail after they arrive</h2>\n<ul class=\"check-list\">\n<li><strong>Slow response.</strong> A lead called the next day has often already spoken to two competitors.</li>\n<li><strong>No record of outcomes.</strong> If sales doesn\'t mark results, campaigns can\'t be improved beyond form counts.</li>\n<li><strong>One call and done.</strong> Many people don\'t answer the first call from an unknown number. A planned sequence of calls and messages over a few days recovers many of them.</li>\n<li><strong>Form too easy.</strong> A one-tap form brings volume, not intent.</li>\n<li><strong>Offer too vague.</strong> \"Contact us for more details\" gives nobody a reason to act.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>What you need to bring</h2>\n<p>An ad budget that you are comfortable testing with for at least two to three months, access to your website and ad accounts (owned by your business, not us), someone who will follow up leads the same day, and a willingness to share honest sales outcomes. We handle the rest.</p>\n\n<h2>Who should not hire us for this</h2>\n<p>If you want a fixed number of leads guaranteed at a fixed price, we are the wrong agency. Anyone promising that is usually either buying data or counting junk. Lead generation is also a poor fit if you have no capacity to follow up, if your offer is not yet clear, or if your business depends on one or two very large contracts a year that come through personal networks rather than search or social.</p>\n\n<h2>Questions business owners ask us</h2>\n<h3>Do you sell databases or ready lead lists?</h3>\n<p>No. We generate enquiries from people who have actively responded to your ads, website or profile. Purchased lists produce poor results and raise consent and privacy problems.</p>\n<h3>Which is better for leads: Google or Facebook?</h3>\n<p>It depends on whether people search for what you sell. If they do, Google Search usually brings higher intent. If they don\'t yet know they need it, Meta can create demand. Many Gurugram businesses use both, with different jobs for each.</p>\n<h3>How much should we spend on ads?</h3>\n<p>It depends on your market, the competition for your keywords, and what a customer is worth to you. We suggest a starting budget after the consultation and adjust it once we see real cost per qualified lead. Our management fee is separate and quoted as a fixed amount after a free consultation.</p>\n<h3>Can you connect leads to our existing CRM?</h3>\n<p>In most cases yes. Common CRMs can receive leads from Meta, Google, LinkedIn and website forms, either directly or through an integration tool. If you don\'t have a CRM, we can set up a simple one or a shared sheet to begin with.</p>\n<h3>We are in Gurgaon but sell across India. Does that matter?</h3>\n<p>Not at all. Campaigns can target any region. Being local simply means it is easy to meet in person and sit with your sales team when needed.</p>\n\n<p>If you are spending on ads and not sure what is actually turning into sales, bring your last few months of lead data to our office in Spaze I-Tech Park on Sohna Road, Sector 49, or call +91 9050126213. <a href=\"/contact-us\">Book a free consultation</a> and we will go through where your leads come from and where they are being lost.</p>', meta_title='Lead Generation Services in Gurugram | TopWebExpert', meta_description='Lead generation built around qualified enquiries: lead definition, tracking, landing pages, Google, Meta and LinkedIn ads, and CRM follow-up in Gurugram.', meta_keywords='lead generation services gurugram, lead generation company gurgaon, b2b lead generation gurgaon, google ads lead generation, facebook lead ads agency', updated_at=NOW(), tier=1 WHERE service_slug='lead-generation' AND location_id=(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE slug='gurgaon' LIMIT 1);
UPDATE city_pages SET title='Local SEO Services in Gurugram', content='<p>In Gurugram, people rarely search for a service \"in the city\". They search by sector, by landmark or simply \"near me\": \"dentist Sector 57\", \"physiotherapist near Sohna Road\", \"cafe near Cyber Hub\", or a Hinglish query like \"AC repair wala near me\". Google answers most of these with the map pack, the three businesses shown on a map above the regular results. Local SEO is the work of making sure your business appears there, and on the organic results below it, for the people who are actually close enough to become customers.</p>\n\n<p>This page explains how we approach local SEO from our office on Sohna Road in Sector 49, what the work includes, and how to tell whether it is working.</p>\n\n<h2>How Local Search Works in a City Built on Sectors</h2>\n\n<p>Google ranks local results on three broad factors: <strong>relevance</strong> (does your business match the search), <strong>distance</strong> (how close you are to the searcher or the place named in the search) and <strong>prominence</strong> (how well known and well reviewed you are). You cannot change distance, but you can change the other two.</p>\n\n<p>Gurugram makes this interesting for a few reasons:</p>\n\n<ul class=\"check-list\">\n<li><strong>Short search radius:</strong> in dense areas such as Golf Course Road or Sector 29, a clinic or restaurant may only show in the map pack for searchers within a small area. A business in New Gurgaon along Dwarka Expressway faces less competition but also fewer searches.</li>\n<li><strong>Sector names in queries:</strong> people type sector numbers, society names and landmarks. Your website and profile should mention the sectors you actually serve, in natural sentences, not in a stuffed list.</li>\n<li><strong>Enquiries move to WhatsApp:</strong> many searchers tap a website, then message on WhatsApp instead of filling a form. If that path is not tracked, local SEO looks weaker than it really is.</li>\n<li><strong>Service-area businesses:</strong> home services, pest control and packers and movers often serve all of Gurugram without a storefront. Google has specific rules for how these businesses should set up their profiles.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>What Our Local SEO Work Covers</h2>\n\n<p>Local SEO is broader than a Google Business Profile. Our work usually includes:</p>\n\n<ul class=\"tag-list\">\n<li>Google Business Profile setup and optimization</li>\n<li>NAP consistency (name, address, phone)</li>\n<li>Local citations and directories</li>\n<li>Location and service page content</li>\n<li>LocalBusiness schema markup</li>\n<li>Review generation process</li>\n<li>Local links and mentions</li>\n<li>Call, form and WhatsApp tracking</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p><strong>Citations</strong> are listings of your business on sites such as Justdial, Sulekha, IndiaMART, Practo (for doctors), Zomato (for restaurants), and industry or RWA directories. The details must match your Google profile exactly. A common Gurugram problem is an old address from before a move, or a listing that still shows a personal mobile number of a former employee.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Location content</strong> is done carefully. If you have one clinic, you need one strong location page, not twenty sector pages with the name swapped. If you have three branches, each gets its own page with the actual address, directions from nearby landmarks, parking details, timings, the doctors or staff at that branch and photos of that location.</p>\n\n<h2>Deliverables and Timeline</h2>\n\n<ol class=\"steps\">\n<li><strong>Week 1: Local audit.</strong> We check your profile, run a map-pack visibility grid around your location, list every citation we can find and note inconsistencies, and review your website\'s local signals.</li>\n<li><strong>Weeks 2-3: Clean-up.</strong> Profile corrections, duplicate listing removal requests, citation fixes on the major directories, and schema markup on the website.</li>\n<li><strong>Weeks 3-6: Content and pages.</strong> Rewriting the location or contact page, adding service pages where they are missing, and linking them from the profile.</li>\n<li><strong>Week 4 onward: Reviews and posts.</strong> A simple process for asking customers for reviews, usually a QR code at the counter and a WhatsApp message template, plus regular profile updates.</li>\n<li><strong>Monthly: Report and adjust.</strong> Visibility grid comparison, profile performance data and enquiry tracking.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h2>What You Need to Provide</h2>\n\n<ul class=\"check-list\">\n<li>Owner or manager access to your Google Business Profile, or help verifying it</li>\n<li>The exact business name as shown on your signboard and documents</li>\n<li>Logins for directory listings you already control, if any</li>\n<li>Real photos of your premises, team and work; stock photos do not help</li>\n<li>A staff member who will ask satisfied customers for reviews</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>Measuring Local Visibility</h2>\n\n<p>Local rankings change street by street, so a single \"rank\" number can mislead. We use:</p>\n\n<ul class=\"check-list\">\n<li><strong>Grid-based rank tracking:</strong> checking your map-pack position from points spread across your service area, so you can see where you appear and where you drop off</li>\n<li><strong>Google Business Profile performance data:</strong> searches, calls, direction requests and website clicks</li>\n<li><strong>Search Console:</strong> impressions and clicks for local queries to your website</li>\n<li><strong>GA4 events:</strong> calls, forms and WhatsApp clicks from organic and profile traffic</li>\n<li><strong>Review count and rating trend</strong> compared with the competitors around you</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>Common Local SEO Mistakes</h2>\n\n<ul class=\"check-list\">\n<li>Adding keywords to the business name on Google, such as \"XYZ Clinic - Dentist Implants Gurugram\". It breaks Google\'s guidelines and can lead to suspension.</li>\n<li>Using a virtual office or co-working address to appear in more areas. Google may remove the listing.</li>\n<li>Buying reviews or having staff post them. These get filtered, and a sudden burst of reviews can trigger scrutiny.</li>\n<li>Ignoring negative reviews instead of replying calmly and factually.</li>\n<li>Changing phone numbers without updating directories and the website.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>Who This Is Not For</h2>\n\n<p>Local SEO helps businesses whose customers are nearby. It is not a good fit for a purely online brand shipping across India, an export house in Manesar that sells to overseas buyers, or a company that has no physical address or defined service area. If that is you, regular SEO or paid campaigns will do more.</p>\n\n<h2>Local SEO Questions We Get Asked</h2>\n\n<h3>Can you get us into the map pack for all of Gurugram?</h3>\n<p>Not realistically for most businesses. Distance is a strong ranking factor, so a clinic in Sector 49 is unlikely to show for searchers near Dwarka Expressway. We focus on winning the area you can serve well and extend reach through website content and reviews.</p>\n\n<h3>We moved from Sector 14 to Sohna Road. Will we lose our rankings?</h3>\n<p>You may see a dip while Google updates your location. Updating the profile address correctly, fixing directory listings and updating your website quickly keeps the disruption short.</p>\n\n<h3>Do Hinglish searches need separate pages?</h3>\n<p>No. Google understands most Hinglish queries and maps them to the same intent. Writing in plain English with the words your customers actually use, and replying to reviews naturally, covers it.</p>\n\n<h3>How much does local SEO cost?</h3>\n<p>It depends on the number of locations, how messy existing listings are, and how much website content is needed. After a free local audit we give you a fixed quote with a clear list of what is included.</p>\n\n<h3>How soon can we see a change?</h3>\n<p>Profile and citation fixes often show within a few weeks in profile performance data. Stronger map-pack positions build over a few months as reviews and content accumulate.</p>\n\n<p>If you want to see how your business appears to people searching around you, <a href=\"/contact-us\">ask for a free local visibility audit</a>. Visit us at Tower B1, Spaze I-Tech Park on Sohna Road, Sector 49, call +91 9050126213 or email info@topwebexpert.com.</p>', meta_title='Local SEO Services in Gurugram | TopWebExpert', meta_description='Local SEO for Gurugram shops, clinics and service firms: map pack visibility by sector, citation clean-up, reviews and call and WhatsApp tracking.', meta_keywords='local seo gurugram, local seo services gurgaon, near me seo, google maps ranking gurugram, local seo agency', updated_at=NOW(), tier=1 WHERE service_slug='local-seo' AND location_id=(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE slug='gurgaon' LIMIT 1);
UPDATE city_pages SET title='Logo Design & Branding', content='<p>A logo has a harder job than most people expect. The same mark has to work on a glass signboard, as a tiny WhatsApp profile picture, as a browser favicon, embroidered on a staff uniform, printed in one colour on a GST invoice and stamped on packaging. A logo that looks great in a presentation but turns into a blur at 32 pixels is not finished. At TopWebExpert we design logos and brand identities for startups and established businesses across Gurugram, and we design with those real uses in mind from the first sketch.</p>\n\n<h2>Where Your Logo Will Actually Live</h2>\n<p>Before we draw anything, we list every place the logo needs to appear. For a D2C brand that means the Instagram grid, Amazon or Flipkart listings, courier boxes and a Shopify favicon. For a clinic on Golf Course Road it means a lit sign, appointment slips, doctor coats and Google Maps. For a real estate developer launching along Dwarka Expressway it means hoardings seen from a moving car, site banners and brochures. For a coaching institute it means student ID cards, YouTube thumbnails and a banner outside a busy market. Each context sets rules on shape, detail and colour, and we test against them.</p>\n\n<h2>Logo Only, or a Full Brand Identity?</h2>\n<p>Not every business needs the full package. We offer two levels of work:</p>\n<ul class=\"check-list\">\n<li><strong>Logo design:</strong> the primary logo, a stacked or horizontal version, an icon mark, colour and single-colour versions, and a one-page usage sheet. Right for a new business that needs to start trading.</li>\n<li><strong>Brand identity:</strong> everything above plus a colour palette with print and screen values, typography, patterns or graphic elements, business cards, letterhead, email signature, social media templates and a brand guidelines document. Right for a business that will have several people or agencies producing material.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>How the Work Unfolds</h2>\n<ol class=\"steps\">\n<li><strong>Week 1: Brand workshop.</strong> A session at our Sohna Road office in Sector 49 or on a video call. We cover who your customers are, what you want to be known for, competitors you want to stand apart from, and words that describe your brand. You get a written creative brief to approve.</li>\n<li><strong>Week 2: Concepts.</strong> We explore many directions on paper and in Adobe Illustrator, then present two to three distinct concepts shown in real mock-ups, not on a white background.</li>\n<li><strong>Weeks 3–4: Refinement.</strong> You pick one direction and we refine it over agreed revision rounds: proportions, spacing, colour and type.</li>\n<li><strong>Weeks 4–6: Identity system and handover.</strong> For brand identity projects, we build the supporting elements and guidelines, then deliver the full file pack.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>A logo-only project usually takes three to four weeks. A full brand identity usually takes five to six, depending on how quickly feedback comes back.</p>\n\n<h2>The Final File Pack</h2>\n<p>You receive every version in the formats your printers, developers and marketing team will ask for:</p>\n<ul class=\"tag-list\">\n<li>AI (Illustrator source)</li>\n<li>SVG</li>\n<li>EPS</li>\n<li>PDF (print-ready)</li>\n<li>PNG with transparent background</li>\n<li>JPG</li>\n<li>Favicon and app icon sizes</li>\n<li>Social media profile sizes</li>\n<li>CMYK, RGB, HEX and Pantone references</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>Checking the Mark Before You Commit</h2>\n<p>A logo you cannot protect is a risk. Before finalising, we run a basic search on the IP India public trademark search and look at competitors in your category to reduce the chance of a close conflict. This is a preliminary check, not legal advice, and we recommend that you file the trademark through a qualified trademark attorney once the logo is final. We also check that the fonts used are licensed for commercial use and that no stock elements are included.</p>\n\n<h2>Who Owns the Logo</h2>\n<p>Under Indian copyright law, the designer of a commissioned artwork can remain the first owner of copyright unless rights are assigned, and the assignment must be in writing. So we do not leave it to assumption: once the project is paid for, we give you a signed copyright assignment for the final logo and identity artwork, along with the editable source files. Unused concepts stay with us and are not sold to anyone else as-is.</p>\n\n<h2>How We Check Quality</h2>\n<ul class=\"check-list\">\n<li>The logo is tested at very small sizes, from a favicon to a WhatsApp display picture.</li>\n<li>It is checked in single-colour black and white for stamps, invoices and embroidery.</li>\n<li>It is placed on light, dark and photographic backgrounds.</li>\n<li>Hindi or bilingual versions are checked with native readers when the brand uses Devanagari.</li>\n<li>Print proofs are reviewed before any large print run.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>What We Ask You to Prepare</h2>\n<p>Bring your final business name and tagline if you have one, a short list of competitors, examples of brands you like and dislike (from any industry), and details of where the logo will be used first. Most importantly, decide who has the final say. Logos designed by committee tend to end up safe and forgettable.</p>\n\n<h2>Common Mistakes With Logos</h2>\n<ul class=\"check-list\">\n<li>Putting too much detail or a tagline inside the mark so it cannot shrink.</li>\n<li>Choosing colours that only work on screen and look dull when printed.</li>\n<li>Using a free template or stock icon that competitors can also use.</li>\n<li>Receiving only a JPG, then paying again when a printer asks for a vector file.</li>\n<li>Skipping a trademark check and having to rebrand after launch.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>When We Are Not the Right Choice</h2>\n<p>If you need a logo by tomorrow or want dozens of options to pick from at the lowest possible cost, a template marketplace will suit you better. We are also not a fit if the business name is still undecided; naming should come first, because the logo depends on it.</p>\n\n<h2>Logo Design FAQs</h2>\n<h3>How many concepts and revisions do we get?</h3>\n<p>We present two to three developed concepts and include a fixed number of revision rounds on the chosen one. The exact number is written into your quote so there are no surprises.</p>\n<h3>What decides the cost of a logo?</h3>\n<p>Cost depends on whether you need a logo only or a full identity, how many applications we design, whether bilingual versions are needed, and the research involved. After a free consultation we give you a fixed quote.</p>\n<h3>Can you refresh our existing logo instead of starting again?</h3>\n<p>Yes. If your current logo has recognition, a careful refresh that keeps its core shape and colour is often wiser than a full change.</p>\n<h3>Will you design our signboard and packaging too?</h3>\n<p>We design the artwork for signage, stationery and packaging and can coordinate with your printer or fabricator to make sure the files are used correctly.</p>\n<h3>We are in Manesar, not central Gurugram. Can we still work with you?</h3>\n<p>Of course. Many clients join the workshop by video, and for businesses anywhere in Gurgaon or Manesar a visit to our office is a short drive.</p>\n\n<p>If you are looking for logo design in Gurugram, visit us at Tower B1, Spaze I-Tech Park, Sohna Road, Sector 49, or call +91 9050126213. <a href=\"/contact-us\">Book a free consultation</a> and bring any rough ideas or references you have. We will help you turn them into a clear brief.</p>', meta_title='Logo Design & Branding in Gurugram | TopWebExpert', meta_description='Logos and brand identities from Gurugram, tested for signboards, WhatsApp and print. Full vector files plus written copyright assignment. Free consultation.', meta_keywords='logo design gurugram, logo designer gurgaon, brand identity design gurugram, branding agency gurugram, business logo design india', updated_at=NOW(), tier=1 WHERE service_slug='logo-design' AND location_id=(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE slug='gurgaon' LIMIT 1);
UPDATE city_pages SET title='Real Estate Digital Marketing', content='<p>Gurugram\'s property market is crowded in a very specific way. Several new projects often launch in the same stretch at the same time, whether along Dwarka Expressway, Golf Course Extension Road or Sohna Road, and they all target the same buyers with similar ads. A buyer searching for a 3 BHK in New Gurgaon can see ten brochures in a week. In that situation, the job of digital marketing is not simply to \"generate leads\". It is to find genuine buyers, get them to a site visit, and keep the sales team from wasting time on the rest.</p>\n<p>TopWebExpert runs real estate digital marketing in Gurugram from our office on Sohna Road in Sector 49, a short drive from many of the new launches in the area. This page explains how we plan campaigns around a project\'s stage, what the compliance requirements are, and what a developer or channel partner should expect from us.</p>\n\n<h2>Who we work with, and how the work differs</h2>\n<p><strong>Developers</strong> usually need the full picture: a project website or landing pages, search and social campaigns, and lead routing to an in-house sales team and to channel partners. <strong>Channel partners</strong> handling mandates for several projects need fast, low-cost landing pages per project and tight lead tracking, because their margin depends on it. <strong>Independent brokers</strong> dealing in resale and rentals in areas like Sushant Lok, DLF Phases or Sector 56 need a different approach: local search visibility, a Google Business Profile and listing-portal management, rather than big ad budgets.</p>\n\n<h2>Compliance comes first</h2>\n<p>Property advertising in Haryana is regulated, and ads that break the rules put the project and the advertiser at risk. Before any campaign goes live we check:</p>\n<ul class=\"check-list\">\n<li>The project is registered with HARERA (Gurugram), and its registration number is shown on every ad, landing page and brochure, along with the authority\'s website where required.</li>\n<li>Channel partners and brokers advertising the project hold their own RERA agent registration and display it.</li>\n<li>Claims such as possession dates, amenities, distances and approvals match what is registered and what the developer can document.</li>\n<li>Price mentions are clear about what is and isn\'t included, so they do not mislead.</li>\n<li>Pre-launch \"EOI\" campaigns for projects that are not yet registered are handled with care. We do not run ads that sell or take bookings for an unregistered project.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>We also follow Google\'s and Meta\'s own advertising policies, which reject ads for vague or misleading property claims.</p>\n\n<h2>Campaigns by project stage</h2>\n<h3>Pre-launch and launch</h3>\n<p>This is when demand is highest and competition is fiercest. We build a fast-loading landing page with floor plans, the location map, price band and RERA details, then run Google Search campaigns on project and location searches, plus Meta campaigns with lead forms to reach buyers who aren\'t searching yet. Budgets usually peak here, and lead volume is watched daily.</p>\n<h3>Sustenance</h3>\n<p>After launch interest fades, inventory still needs to move. We shift towards remarketing to past site visitors, construction update videos, specific unit types that are left, and search campaigns on narrower terms. Cost per lead often rises, so lead quality becomes the main focus.</p>\n<h3>Ready to move in</h3>\n<p>For completed or near-complete projects, the selling point is certainty. We use walkthrough videos, photos of the actual site, possession details and nearby infrastructure. Search terms like \"ready to move flats\" plus a sector or road perform well at this stage.</p>\n\n<h2>Where the enquiries come from</h2>\n<ul class=\"tag-list\">\n<li>Google Search ads</li>\n<li>Meta lead forms</li>\n<li>Instagram Reels</li>\n<li>YouTube walkthroughs</li>\n<li>Landing page forms</li>\n<li>Click-to-WhatsApp ads</li>\n<li>Google Business Profile</li>\n<li>Property portals</li>\n</ul>\n<p>We don\'t use every channel for every project. A luxury project on Golf Course Road and an affordable housing project in Sohna need very different mixes, and we plan the split with you based on buyer profile and budget.</p>\n\n<h2>The follow-up problem</h2>\n<p>In our experience, the biggest leak in property marketing is not the ads. It is what happens after the form is submitted. Meta lead forms in particular bring many people who tapped \"submit\" without much thought, and if a sales executive calls them the next day, the interest has gone.</p>\n<ol class=\"steps\">\n<li>Every lead is pushed instantly into your CRM (or a shared sheet if you don\'t have one yet), tagged with the source, campaign and project.</li>\n<li>An automatic WhatsApp or SMS goes out within minutes with the brochure and a site visit booking link.</li>\n<li>The lead is assigned to a salesperson, who is expected to call quickly. We track how fast that happens.</li>\n<li>Sales marks each lead as not reachable, not interested, budget mismatch, visit booked, visit done or booked unit.</li>\n<li>We use those statuses to cut campaigns and audiences that bring poor leads, even if their cost per lead looks cheap.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>This requires honest feedback from your sales team. Without it, we can only optimise for form fills, which is not the same as buyers.</p>\n\n<h2>What you receive each month</h2>\n<ul class=\"check-list\">\n<li>Campaign management on the agreed platforms, with daily budget checks during launch periods.</li>\n<li>New ad creatives and copy as inventory, offers or construction stages change.</li>\n<li>Landing page updates, including price, payment plan and availability changes.</li>\n<li>A report showing leads, cost per lead, cost per site visit and, where your CRM allows, cost per booking, broken down by channel.</li>\n<li>A review call with recommendations for the next month.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>What we need from you: approved creatives or brand guidelines, RERA details, floor plans, price sheets, a named person who can approve ads quickly, and access to lead statuses in your CRM.</p>\n\n<h2>When we are not the right fit</h2>\n<p>We are probably not right for you if you want campaigns for a project without RERA registration, if you want to run ads with a price or possession date the developer hasn\'t confirmed, or if your team cannot follow up leads within the same day. We are also not a listing portal. We don\'t sell pre-verified buyer data, and we\'d advise you to be careful with anyone who does.</p>\n\n<h2>FAQ</h2>\n<h3>Why are my Facebook property leads so poor?</h3>\n<p>Usually the form is too easy to submit, the audience is too broad, or the follow-up is slow. Adding a qualifying question (budget or unit type), switching to a higher-intent form type and calling within minutes normally improves quality. We check which of these is the problem in your account.</p>\n<h3>Should a channel partner run ads on a developer\'s project name?</h3>\n<p>Many do, but check your mandate agreement first. Some developers restrict bidding on the project name or require approved creatives. We follow whatever your agreement allows.</p>\n<h3>How long before we see site visits?</h3>\n<p>Search campaigns can start producing enquiries within days of going live. Site visits depend on your follow-up and the project\'s appeal, and the first few weeks are used to learn which channels and audiences bring serious buyers.</p>\n<h3>How is the budget decided?</h3>\n<p>It depends on the project\'s price segment, how many competing launches are nearby, the number of units to sell and the timeline. Ad spend is separate from our management fee. We give a fixed quote for our work after a free consultation.</p>\n<h3>Do you handle projects outside Gurugram?</h3>\n<p>Yes. Our focus, though, is Gurugram and its surrounding markets, including Sohna, Manesar and Dwarka Expressway, because being close by helps us understand the micro-markets buyers compare.</p>\n\n<p>If you are planning a launch or want to fix an existing campaign, meet us at our office in Spaze I-Tech Park on Sohna Road, Sector 49, or call +91 9050126213. <a href=\"/contact-us\">Book a free consultation</a> and bring your current lead reports; we will tell you where the leaks are.</p>', meta_title='Real Estate Digital Marketing Gurugram | TopWebExpert', meta_description='Property marketing for Gurugram developers and channel partners: HARERA-compliant ads, launch campaigns, landing pages and CRM follow-up for site visits.', meta_keywords='real estate digital marketing gurugram, real estate marketing agency gurgaon, property leads gurgaon, real estate lead generation, channel partner marketing', updated_at=NOW(), tier=1 WHERE service_slug='real-estate-marketing' AND location_id=(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE slug='gurgaon' LIMIT 1);
UPDATE city_pages SET title='Search Engine Optimization Services in Gurugram', content='<p>Most Gurugram businesses that call us about SEO already have a website, a few blog posts and a vague sense that \"nothing is happening\". Usually the problem is not effort. The site is slow on mobile, service pages compete with each other for the same keywords, or the content is written for the owner rather than for the person searching. Our SEO work fixes those foundations first and then builds visibility for the searches that actually bring enquiries.</p>\n\n<p>We are a Gurugram agency with an office on Sohna Road in Sector 49. Over 7+ years we have worked with 150+ clients on 500+ projects. Search in this city is crowded and varied, from SaaS teams in Cyber City competing nationally to clinics off Golf Course Extension Road competing for patients within a few kilometres, and each needs a different plan.</p>\n\n<h2>What SEO Work Actually Involves</h2>\n\n<p>\"SEO\" gets sold as a monthly package of backlinks and blog posts. In practice, organic search depends on three layers, and we work on them in this order:</p>\n\n<ul class=\"check-list\">\n<li><strong>Technical health:</strong> crawlability, indexing, site speed, Core Web Vitals on mobile, redirects, canonical tags, structured data and XML sitemaps. If Google cannot crawl and understand a page, nothing else matters.</li>\n<li><strong>Page and content relevance:</strong> one clear page per service or topic, written around what buyers actually search, with proper titles, headings, internal links and answers to real questions.</li>\n<li><strong>Authority:</strong> mentions and links from relevant sites such as industry associations, supplier and partner sites, local publications and genuine PR. We do not buy links from networks, because those tend to cause problems later.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>For a B2B software company targeting buyers across India, most of the effort goes into content and authority. For a hospital or a coaching institute, the technical and page layers plus local signals usually matter more. The plan depends on the business, which is why we start with an audit instead of a package.</p>\n\n<h2>The First 12 Weeks, Step by Step</h2>\n\n<ol class=\"steps\">\n<li><strong>Weeks 1-2: Audit and keyword mapping.</strong> We crawl the site, review Search Console data, check indexing and speed, and study which competitors rank for your key searches. You get a written audit and a keyword map that assigns each target search to one page.</li>\n<li><strong>Weeks 3-5: Technical fixes.</strong> We fix or brief your developer on crawl errors, broken redirects, duplicate pages, slow templates and missing structured data. If we built your site, we make the changes ourselves.</li>\n<li><strong>Weeks 5-8: Page rewrites and new pages.</strong> Existing service pages are rewritten or merged, and missing pages are created where the keyword map shows a gap. Each page gets a clear title, description and internal links.</li>\n<li><strong>Weeks 8-12: Content and authority.</strong> We start publishing articles that answer buyer questions and begin outreach for relevant mentions and links.</li>\n<li><strong>Week 12: Review.</strong> We compare impressions, clicks, rankings and enquiries against the baseline and agree the plan for the next quarter.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<p>Technical fixes often show in Search Console within a few weeks. Ranking movement for competitive commercial searches usually takes several months, and we will say so upfront rather than promise page-one positions by a date.</p>\n\n<h2>What We Need From You</h2>\n\n<p>SEO moves faster when the client team is involved. Before we start, we ask for:</p>\n\n<ul class=\"check-list\">\n<li>Admin or editor access to the website, plus hosting or developer contact if we did not build it</li>\n<li>Owner access to Google Search Console and Google Analytics 4, or permission to set them up</li>\n<li>A list of your most profitable services and the areas or customer types you want more of</li>\n<li>Someone who can review content for accuracy within a few working days, especially for medical, legal or financial topics</li>\n<li>Photos, project details and real FAQs from your sales or front-desk team</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>How We Report Progress</h2>\n\n<p>Every month you receive a short report and a call. We track numbers you can verify yourself in your own accounts:</p>\n\n<ul class=\"tag-list\">\n<li>Search Console impressions and clicks</li>\n<li>Average position for mapped keywords</li>\n<li>Indexed vs excluded pages</li>\n<li>GA4 organic sessions</li>\n<li>Form submissions and click-to-call events</li>\n<li>WhatsApp button clicks</li>\n<li>Core Web Vitals</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>Rankings are useful, but enquiries are what pay the bills. That is why we set up GA4 events for forms, calls and WhatsApp clicks in the first month, so organic traffic can be tied to leads rather than just visits.</p>\n\n<h2>Mistakes We Often See on Gurugram Websites</h2>\n\n<p>After auditing many local sites, a few patterns come up again and again:</p>\n\n<ul class=\"check-list\">\n<li><strong>Dozens of near-identical location pages:</strong> \"service in Sector 45\", \"service in Sector 46\" and so on, each with a swapped name. Google now treats these as low-value doorway pages, and they can drag down the whole site.</li>\n<li><strong>Heavy homepage sliders and uncompressed images:</strong> common on real estate and interior design sites. They look good on office Wi-Fi but load slowly on a phone in traffic on MG Road.</li>\n<li><strong>Blog posts with no link to a service page:</strong> traffic arrives, reads, and leaves without any path to enquire.</li>\n<li><strong>Changing domains or redesigning without redirects:</strong> years of rankings can disappear in a week.</li>\n<li><strong>Buying cheap backlink packages:</strong> these rarely help and can trigger manual actions.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>When SEO Is the Wrong Choice</h2>\n\n<p>We would rather tell you now than take a retainer that will disappoint you. SEO is probably not the right first investment if:</p>\n\n<ul class=\"check-list\">\n<li>You need leads this month for a launch or a limited-time offer. Paid ads are faster.</li>\n<li>Your business is a single event or a short-term project with no ongoing demand.</li>\n<li>You cannot give access to the website or approve content changes.</li>\n<li>Your website is about to be rebuilt. In that case, plan SEO into the rebuild rather than optimizing a site that will be replaced.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>For a steady business that wants enquiries that do not stop the day the ad budget runs out, organic search is worth the patience.</p>\n\n<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>\n\n<h3>How long before we see results from SEO?</h3>\n<p>Technical fixes and improved page titles can show changes in Search Console impressions within a few weeks. Meaningful growth in rankings and enquiries for competitive searches typically takes several months. The timeline depends on your site\'s current state and how competitive your industry is in Gurugram and beyond.</p>\n\n<h3>Do you guarantee first-page rankings?</h3>\n<p>No. Nobody controls Google\'s rankings, and agencies that guarantee positions are usually targeting keywords nobody searches. We commit to clear work, a documented plan and honest reporting from your own Search Console and GA4 data.</p>\n\n<h3>How much does SEO cost?</h3>\n<p>Cost depends on the size of your site, how much technical work is needed, how many services you want to rank for and how much content has to be written. We give a fixed monthly quote after a free audit, so you know exactly what is included.</p>\n\n<h3>We are in Udyog Vihar but sell across India. Is local SEO or regular SEO better for us?</h3>\n<p>If your customers are nationwide, you need regular SEO focused on topics and services, not on the city. Local SEO matters when customers come to you or you serve a defined area. Many businesses need a mix, and the audit will show which.</p>\n\n<h3>Can you work with our existing developer?</h3>\n<p>Yes. We share a prioritized list of technical fixes with clear instructions and check the changes after they go live. Many clients keep their developer and use us for SEO strategy, content and reporting.</p>\n\n<p>If you want an honest view of where your site stands, <a href=\"/contact-us\">book a free SEO audit</a>. Our office is in Spaze I-Tech Park on Sohna Road, Sector 49, so meeting in person is easy for businesses in south Gurugram, and we are happy to work over video calls for teams in Cyber City, Gurgaon\'s older sectors or anywhere else. Call +91 9050126213 or email info@topwebexpert.com.</p>', meta_title='SEO Services in Gurugram | TopWebExpert', meta_description='SEO for Gurugram businesses: technical audit, keyword mapping, page rewrites and honest monthly reporting from Search Console and GA4. Free audit first.', meta_keywords='seo services gurugram, seo company in gurgaon, seo agency gurugram, website seo audit, search engine optimization gurugram', updated_at=NOW(), tier=1 WHERE service_slug='search-engine-optimization' AND location_id=(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE slug='gurgaon' LIMIT 1);
UPDATE city_pages SET title='Shopify Development in Gurugram', content='<p>Shopify lets a brand start selling without worrying about servers, updates or security patches. That is why many young D2C brands in Gurugram, selling apparel, skincare, home decor or packaged food, choose it. But a Shopify store set up with default settings is not ready for Indian buyers. Payments, COD, GST, shipping and speed all need attention. We set up, customise and migrate Shopify stores from our office on Sohna Road, and this page explains what that involves.</p><h2>Is Shopify the right platform for you?</h2><h3>Shopify fits well if</h3><ul class=\"check-list\"><li>You sell physical products to consumers and want to launch in weeks, not months.</li><li>You would rather pay a monthly subscription than manage hosting, updates and security.</li><li>Your team is non-technical and needs a simple admin panel for products, orders and discounts.</li><li>You plan to grow through Instagram, Meta and Google ads, and want solid tracking and catalogue sync.</li></ul><h3>Look at other options if</h3><ul class=\"check-list\"><li>You need complex B2B pricing, dealer-specific catalogues or credit terms. WooCommerce or a custom build may cost less over time.</li><li>Your products are mainly services, bookings or course enrolments.</li><li>You want total control over URLs and server behaviour. Shopify uses set URL patterns, such as /products/ and /collections/, that cannot be changed.</li><li>Monthly app subscriptions, many billed in US dollars, would strain your budget.</li></ul><h2>Making Shopify work for Indian buyers</h2><p>Most of our Shopify work is here, rather than in the design:</p><ul class=\"check-list\"><li><strong>Payments.</strong> We connect an Indian gateway such as Razorpay, PayU or Cashfree so buyers can pay by UPI, cards, net banking and wallets, and we test the full flow including failed and refunded payments.</li><li><strong>Cash on delivery.</strong> Set up as a manual payment method, with rules or apps to limit it by order value or pincode and to confirm COD orders before dispatch.</li><li><strong>GST.</strong> Tax-inclusive pricing configured correctly, HSN codes added to products, and a GST invoice app so each order produces a compliant invoice.</li><li><strong>Shipping.</strong> Integration with Shiprocket or Delhivery for labels, pickups and tracking, plus a pincode checker on product pages.</li><li><strong>Order updates.</strong> Confirmation and shipping messages on WhatsApp as well as email, since many buyers check WhatsApp first.</li></ul><h2>Theme choice: free, premium or custom</h2><p>Every Online Store 2.0 theme, including Shopify\'s free Dawn theme, lets you rearrange sections without code. For many new brands, a well-chosen theme with custom styling and a few custom Liquid sections is enough, and it keeps costs and load times down. A premium theme from the Shopify Theme Store adds ready-made features for a one-time licence fee. A fully custom theme makes sense when your brand needs layouts or product experiences that no theme offers, such as a build-your-own gift box or a detailed size guide per product type. We show you options side by side and explain what each one changes.</p><h2>Apps we commonly work with</h2><ul class=\"tag-list\"><li>Razorpay</li><li>Cashfree</li><li>Shiprocket</li><li>Delhivery</li><li>Judge.me reviews</li><li>Shopify Search &amp; Discovery</li><li>Shopify Email</li><li>Google &amp; YouTube channel</li><li>Facebook &amp; Instagram channel</li></ul><p>Every app adds scripts that can slow your store. We install only what you need and remove leftover code when an app is uninstalled.</p><h2>From sign-up to first order</h2><ol class=\"steps\"><li><strong>Store set-up</strong> (week 1): Shopify account in your name, plan selection, domain connection, taxes, shipping zones and policies.</li><li><strong>Theme and design</strong> (weeks 1 to 3): home, collection and product page designs, then theme customisation.</li><li><strong>Products and collections</strong> (weeks 2 to 3): bulk import from your spreadsheet, variants, images, filters and SEO fields.</li><li><strong>Payments, shipping and apps</strong> (weeks 3 to 4): gateway, COD rules, courier integration, invoices and notifications.</li><li><strong>Test orders and launch</strong> (week 4 or 5): real orders on every payment method, then removing the store password.</li></ol><p>A store with a ready product list usually goes live in 3 to 5 weeks. A fully custom theme or a migration adds time.</p><h2>Moving from WooCommerce or another platform</h2><p>We migrate products, customers and past orders, then rebuild navigation and collections. Because Shopify uses its own URL structure, every old product and category URL is redirected to its new address so your search rankings and ad links keep working. Customer passwords cannot be carried across, so we plan an account re-activation email for your existing buyers.</p><h2>What you need to provide</h2><p>A product sheet with titles, prices, variants, weights and HSN codes; product and lifestyle photos; your logo and brand guidelines; business documents for gateway KYC; and written return and shipping policies. You also need to add your own payment method to the Shopify account, since the subscription is billed to you.</p><h2>Running costs to plan for</h2><p>We give a fixed quote for our work after a free consultation. Separately, budget for the Shopify plan, any transaction fees Shopify charges on your plan, your payment gateway\'s charges, monthly app subscriptions and a premium theme licence if you choose one. We list all of these in writing before you commit, so the monthly bill holds no surprises.</p><h2>What we check before your store goes live</h2><ul class=\"check-list\"><li>Mobile PageSpeed and Core Web Vitals on the home, collection and product pages.</li><li>Checkout tested on UPI, cards and COD on a real phone over mobile data.</li><li>GST invoice output checked for orders within Haryana and outside it.</li><li>Staff accounts with only the permissions each person needs, and two-step login switched on.</li><li>Google Analytics, Search Console and Meta pixel events firing correctly.</li></ul><h2>Shopify questions we hear often</h2><h3>Do I own my Shopify store?</h3><p>Yes. The store is opened under your email and billing, and we work as staff or collaborators. You can remove our access at any time.</p><h3>Can I offer cash on delivery on Shopify?</h3><p>Yes. COD is a built-in manual payment option, and we add rules to limit it by order value or pincode, plus a confirmation step to cut down on fake orders.</p><h3>Can Shopify generate GST invoices?</h3><p>Yes, through an invoice app configured with your GSTIN, HSN codes and state-wise tax split. We recommend your accountant checks a few sample invoices before launch.</p><h3>Will my store be slow because of apps?</h3><p>It can be if apps pile up. We keep the app list short, test speed after each one, and clean up code left behind by old apps.</p><h3>Can you work on a Shopify store someone else built?</h3><p>Yes. We start by reviewing the theme, apps and settings, then fix the most costly issues first.</p><p>If you run a Shopify store in Gurugram, or are about to launch one, meet us at Tower B1, Spaze I-Tech Park, Sohna Road, Sector 49. It is a short drive from Golf Course Extension Road and the older Gurgaon sectors alike. <a href=\"/contact-us\">Book a free consultation</a> and bring your product list or store link.</p>', meta_title='Shopify Development in Gurugram | TopWebExpert', meta_description='Shopify stores set up for Indian buyers: UPI via Razorpay or Cashfree, COD rules, GST invoices, Shiprocket shipping and theme work. Free consultation.', meta_keywords='shopify development gurugram, shopify developer in gurgaon, shopify store setup gurugram, shopify theme customization gurgaon, woocommerce to shopify migration', updated_at=NOW(), tier=1 WHERE service_slug='shopify-development' AND location_id=(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE slug='gurgaon' LIMIT 1);
UPDATE city_pages SET title='SMS Marketing', content='<p>SMS is not glamorous, but it still does jobs other channels cannot. It reaches phones without internet, it doesn\'t depend on someone having installed an app, and for OTPs, booking confirmations and payment reminders people still expect a text. What has changed in India is the rulebook. Since TRAI brought in DLT (Distributed Ledger Technology) registration, every commercial SMS has to come from a registered business, through a registered sender ID, using a registered template. Messages that don\'t match are silently dropped by the operator.</p>\n<p>Many Gurugram businesses come to us after their SMS \"stopped working\". Usually a template was edited, a link was not whitelisted, or promotional messages were being sent to numbers on the Do Not Disturb list. Our SMS marketing service in Gurugram starts by fixing that foundation and then builds useful campaigns on top of it.</p>\n\n<h2>Four kinds of business SMS, and why the difference matters</h2>\n<p>Under the DLT system, each message falls into a category, and the category decides who you can send it to:</p>\n<ul class=\"check-list\">\n<li><strong>Transactional:</strong> mainly OTPs sent by banks and similar entities. Most small and mid-sized businesses will not use this category.</li>\n<li><strong>Service (implicit):</strong> messages tied to something the customer already did with you, such as an order confirmation, appointment reminder or delivery update. These can reach numbers on the DND list.</li>\n<li><strong>Service (explicit):</strong> messages sent to a customer who has given recorded consent to receive them, even if they are on DND. Consent must be captured and registered in the proper way.</li>\n<li><strong>Promotional:</strong> offers, launches and sale announcements. These are not delivered to numbers registered on the National Customer Preference Register (NCPR), and can only go out during the hours TRAI allows.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Choosing the wrong category is the single biggest reason for poor delivery.</p>\n\n<h2>Getting registered: the DLT checklist</h2>\n<p>If you have never sent commercial SMS before, this is what has to happen before your first campaign. We handle the paperwork with you; the registration itself stays in your company\'s name.</p>\n<ol class=\"steps\">\n<li><strong>Entity registration</strong> on one of the operator DLT portals (for example Jio, Airtel, Vi or BSNL), using your PAN, GST certificate and an authorisation letter. Registration on one portal works across all operators. You receive a Principal Entity ID.</li>\n<li><strong>Header (sender ID) registration.</strong> Service and transactional messages use a short alphabetic header, usually based on your brand name. Promotional messages use a numeric header. Headers that look like another brand get rejected.</li>\n<li><strong>Consent template registration</strong>, if you plan to send explicit service messages to customers who have opted in.</li>\n<li><strong>Content template registration.</strong> Each message is registered with fixed text and marked variables, for example a customer name or a booking date.</li>\n<li><strong>URL and callback number whitelisting.</strong> Links and phone numbers inside messages now need to be whitelisted, and short links must come from an approved source. Unlisted links cause messages to be blocked.</li>\n<li><strong>Provider connection.</strong> Your Entity ID, headers and template IDs are mapped in your SMS gateway, and a test batch is sent to our team\'s phones on different networks.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Approvals usually take a few working days per step. Allow roughly one to two weeks from start to first live message if your documents are ready.</p>\n\n<h2>Where SMS earns its place</h2>\n<p>We recommend SMS for specific uses, not as a general \"send offers to everyone\" tool:</p>\n<ul class=\"tag-list\">\n<li>Appointment reminders</li>\n<li>Order and delivery updates</li>\n<li>Payment and renewal reminders</li>\n<li>Event and site-visit confirmations</li>\n<li>Missed-call follow-ups</li>\n<li>Store launch announcements</li>\n<li>Re-engaging past customers</li>\n</ul>\n<p>For a clinic, a salon or a service business in areas like Sector 49, DLF Phase 4 or Sushant Lok, an automated reminder the day before an appointment is often the most useful message they send. For a restaurant or retail outlet near Cyber Hub or on MG Road, a short promotional SMS to past customers can bring people back on a slow weekday, provided it goes only to non-DND numbers and says something worth reading.</p>\n\n<h2>Writing messages that get read</h2>\n<p>An SMS has little room. A standard English message fits 160 characters per part; a Hindi message in Devanagari (Unicode) fits only 70 per part, so it costs more parts for the same content. We write around a few simple rules: brand name in the first few words, one clear action, one whitelisted link or number, and no ALL CAPS or strings of exclamation marks. Every promotional message tells the recipient how to stop receiving them.</p>\n\n<h2>A typical month with us</h2>\n<ul class=\"check-list\">\n<li>Review last month\'s delivery report by operator and template.</li>\n<li>Clean the contact list: remove numbers that repeatedly fail and anyone who asked to stop.</li>\n<li>Register any new templates needed for upcoming campaigns, well in advance.</li>\n<li>Run the planned promotional sends to the right segments, and monitor automated service messages.</li>\n<li>Check link clicks and, where possible, match them to enquiries or sales in your CRM or billing software.</li>\n<li>Send you a short report with what to keep, change or stop.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>The numbers we look at</h2>\n<p>Success is measured on delivery rate (per operator, since problems often show up on one network first), link click rate, responses such as calls or replies, bookings or sales that can be traced back to a campaign, and cost per lead or per booking. We also track DND exclusions, so you can see how much of your list promotional messages can actually reach.</p>\n\n<h2>Common mistakes we fix</h2>\n<ul class=\"check-list\">\n<li>Editing a message slightly in the gateway so it no longer matches the registered template.</li>\n<li>Using a random URL shortener that is not whitelisted.</li>\n<li>Sending promotions on a service header.</li>\n<li>Buying a number list. Apart from being a poor audience, it exposes you to complaints against your header and entity.</li>\n<li>Sending the same offer so often that people register complaints.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>When not to use SMS</h2>\n<p>SMS is a weak fit if your customers are mostly businesses who prefer email, if your offer needs images or a catalogue to make sense (WhatsApp or email does that better), or if you have no list of existing customers at all. For cold audiences, paid search and social ads are a better starting point, and SMS can follow once people have enquired.</p>\n\n<h2>FAQ</h2>\n<h3>Why are my SMS showing as sent but customers are not receiving them?</h3>\n<p>The usual causes are a template mismatch, a link or number that isn\'t whitelisted, a promotional message going to DND numbers, or the wrong header for that category. We check the delivery report by operator and error code to find which one it is.</p>\n<h3>Do I have to register on DLT myself?</h3>\n<p>The registration must be in your business\'s name, since you are the principal entity. We prepare the documents, fill in the portal with you and register headers and templates, but the account stays yours.</p>\n<h3>Can I send promotional SMS to numbers on DND?</h3>\n<p>No. Promotional messages are not delivered to numbers on the NCPR. You can send service messages related to an existing transaction, or explicit service messages to customers who have given registered consent.</p>\n<h3>What does an SMS campaign cost?</h3>\n<p>Cost depends on the volume of messages, whether they are English or Hindi (Unicode uses more parts), the gateway\'s per-message rate, and how much template work and reporting you need from us. We give a fixed quote after a free consultation.</p>\n<h3>Is SMS better than WhatsApp?</h3>\n<p>Neither is better in general. SMS works without internet and suits short reminders; WhatsApp suits conversations, images and replies. Many businesses in Gurgaon use SMS for reminders and WhatsApp for sales conversations.</p>\n\n<p>If your SMS delivery has dropped, or you want to set up DLT properly from the start, talk to us. Our office is in Spaze I-Tech Park on Sohna Road, Sector 49, and you can reach us on +91 9050126213 or info@topwebexpert.com. <a href=\"/contact-us\">Request a free consultation</a> and we will review your current headers, templates and delivery reports.</p>', meta_title='SMS Marketing in Gurugram with DLT Setup | TopWebExpert', meta_description='DLT-compliant SMS marketing from our Sohna Road office: entity, header and template registration, URL whitelisting, DND rules and campaigns that deliver.', meta_keywords='sms marketing gurugram, bulk sms service gurgaon, dlt registration for sms, promotional sms gurgaon, transactional sms provider', updated_at=NOW(), tier=1 WHERE service_slug='sms-marketing' AND location_id=(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE slug='gurgaon' LIMIT 1);
UPDATE city_pages SET title='Social Media Optimization', content='<p>Before a customer calls you, there is a good chance they look you up on Instagram, LinkedIn or Facebook. A buyer comparing two interior designers, a corporate HR team checking a caterer, or a parent looking at a new play school near Sohna Road will all scroll through your profile to decide whether you look active, trustworthy and professional. If the last post is from eight months ago, the bio is unclear and the contact button is broken, you lose that customer quietly, without ever knowing they were interested.</p>\n<p>Social media optimization (SMO) fixes that. It is the work of making your social profiles complete, consistent, easy to find and easy to act on, and then keeping them active with content that suits a business of your size. This page explains how we approach social media optimization in Gurugram, what you get, and what the work cannot do.</p>\n\n<h2>SMO and paid social are different jobs</h2>\n<p>People often use SMO and social media marketing to mean the same thing. We separate them because they solve different problems:</p>\n<ul class=\"check-list\">\n<li><strong>SMO</strong> improves your organic presence: profile setup, search visibility within each platform, content, posting routine, links to your website, and how you handle comments and messages.</li>\n<li><strong>Paid social</strong> is advertising: you pay Meta or LinkedIn to show content to chosen audiences.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Ads work better when the profile they lead to is in good shape, so SMO is usually the first step. But SMO alone will not bring large numbers of new followers quickly. Organic reach on most platforms is limited, and anyone promising fast follower growth without ads is usually selling fake followers.</p>\n\n<h2>Day one: the profile audit</h2>\n<p>We start by reviewing every account you have, including the ones someone opened years ago and forgot. For each, we check:</p>\n<ol class=\"steps\">\n<li><strong>Ownership and access.</strong> Who has admin rights? Is the page owned by your Meta Business account, or by a former employee\'s personal profile? This is fixed first, because losing access to a business page is common and painful.</li>\n<li><strong>Name and handle.</strong> Is the business name identical across platforms, and is the handle easy to guess and spell?</li>\n<li><strong>Bio and category.</strong> Does the bio say what you do, for whom, and where, in plain words? Is the right business category selected?</li>\n<li><strong>Contact details.</strong> Phone, WhatsApp, email, address and website link all match your Google Business Profile and website.</li>\n<li><strong>Action buttons.</strong> Book, call, WhatsApp or enquiry buttons are set up and tested.</li>\n<li><strong>Highlights, pinned posts and cover images.</strong> A new visitor should understand your services, pricing approach, location and proof of work within a few seconds.</li>\n<li><strong>Duplicate and unofficial pages.</strong> Old or duplicate pages that confuse customers are merged or removed where the platform allows.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>You receive the audit as a simple list of fixes, marked by priority. Most profile fixes are done within the first two weeks.</p>\n\n<h2>Choosing the right platforms</h2>\n<h3>Instagram</h3>\n<p>Suits businesses where visuals sell: restaurants and cafés, fitness studios, salons, fashion, interiors, events and real estate. Reels and a well-organised grid matter more than daily posting.</p>\n<h3>LinkedIn</h3>\n<p>For B2B companies, consultancies, IT and SaaS firms, many of which sit in Cyber City, Udyog Vihar and along Golf Course Road. A company page plus active founder or leadership profiles usually does more than a company page alone.</p>\n<h3>Facebook</h3>\n<p>Still useful for local communities, reviews and older audiences, and it is where your Meta business settings, WhatsApp link and ads are managed.</p>\n<h3>YouTube</h3>\n<p>Worth the effort when your service needs explaining: walkthroughs, tutorials, product demos. Good titles and descriptions make videos findable in search for a long time.</p>\n<p>Most small businesses do better with two platforms done properly than with five done badly. We will recommend which ones to keep, which to pause, and which to close.</p>\n\n<h2>A content routine your team can keep up</h2>\n<p>The main reason business profiles go quiet is that the plan was too ambitious. We build a monthly calendar around what you can realistically supply: a few photos or videos from your team each week, customer questions you already get, updates and offers. Typical content types include:</p>\n<ul class=\"tag-list\">\n<li>Behind-the-scenes</li>\n<li>Answers to common questions</li>\n<li>Before-and-after work</li>\n<li>Team introductions</li>\n<li>Short how-to Reels</li>\n<li>Event and launch updates</li>\n<li>Customer reviews (shared with permission)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Each post is written with searchable words in the caption, a few relevant hashtags rather than thirty, and location tags where it helps local discovery.</p>\n\n<h2>Monthly deliverables</h2>\n<ul class=\"check-list\">\n<li>A content calendar agreed with you before the month starts.</li>\n<li>Design and captions for the agreed number of posts, Reels and stories.</li>\n<li>Scheduling and publishing.</li>\n<li>Monitoring comments and messages, with replies to routine questions and quick escalation of enquiries and complaints to your team.</li>\n<li>Profile upkeep: updated highlights, pinned posts, bio and links.</li>\n<li>A monthly report and a short review call.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>From you, we need one point of contact, raw photos and videos from your premises or projects, quick approvals, and answers when customers ask something we can\'t answer on your behalf.</p>\n\n<h2>What we measure</h2>\n<p>Follower count is reported, but it is not the goal. We look at reach among people in and around Gurugram, saves and shares (a better sign of useful content than likes), profile visits, website link clicks, call and WhatsApp button taps, direct message enquiries, and how quickly those enquiries are answered. Over a few months, these show whether your social presence is actually helping customers choose you.</p>\n\n<h2>Mistakes we see often</h2>\n<ul class=\"check-list\">\n<li>Buying followers or engagement, which damages reach and credibility.</li>\n<li>Posting only offers and festival greetings, with nothing that helps the customer.</li>\n<li>Leaving messages unanswered for days.</li>\n<li>Using a different business name, phone number or address on each platform.</li>\n<li>Letting an agency or freelancer own the page instead of the business.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>When SMO is not the answer</h2>\n<p>If you need sales next month from people who don\'t know you yet, paid advertising or search campaigns will act faster. If nobody in your business can supply photos, answer messages or approve posts, SMO will stall. And if your customers are a handful of large companies reached through tenders or direct sales, a solid LinkedIn presence is enough; a full content calendar would be wasted effort.</p>\n\n<h2>FAQ</h2>\n<h3>How is SMO different from SEO?</h3>\n<p>SEO improves how your website appears in Google search. SMO improves your social profiles and content. They support each other: consistent business details and links across social profiles and your website help customers, and the content can be reused on both.</p>\n<h3>Will you guarantee a number of followers?</h3>\n<p>No. Genuine follower growth depends on your content, your niche and whether you also run ads. We report growth honestly and focus on enquiries and engagement from relevant people.</p>\n<h3>Do we have to appear on camera?</h3>\n<p>It helps, especially for service businesses in Gurgaon where trust in the person matters, but it is not required. Product, workspace and process videos also work well.</p>\n<h3>How much does social media optimization cost?</h3>\n<p>Cost depends on the number of platforms, how many posts and Reels you need each month, whether we shoot content or use yours, and how much message handling is involved. We give a fixed monthly quote after a free consultation.</p>\n<h3>Can you take over accounts another agency set up?</h3>\n<p>Yes. The first step is making sure your business, not the previous agency, holds full admin access. We help you recover access where needed.</p>\n\n<p>Want a second opinion on your current profiles? Visit our office at Spaze I-Tech Park on Sohna Road, Sector 49, or call +91 9050126213. <a href=\"/contact-us\">Book a free consultation</a> and we will walk you through a quick audit of your social accounts, with no obligation.</p>', meta_title='Social Media Optimization in Gurugram | TopWebExpert', meta_description='SMO for Gurugram businesses: profile audits, access recovery, platform choice, a content calendar your team can sustain, and reports on enquiries.', meta_keywords='social media optimization gurugram, smo services gurgaon, smo company gurgaon, instagram profile optimization, linkedin company page optimization', updated_at=NOW(), tier=1 WHERE service_slug='social-media-optimization' AND location_id=(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE slug='gurgaon' LIMIT 1);
UPDATE city_pages SET title='Custom Software Development', content='<p>A lot of businesses in Gurugram run on spreadsheets that have grown too big. A real estate sales team tracks site visits in a shared Excel file. A logistics firm near Manesar dispatches trucks from WhatsApp groups. A coaching institute reconciles fee payments by hand every month. None of this is wrong at the start, but at some point the workarounds cost more than a proper system would. That is the point where custom software makes sense, and it is the work we do at TopWebExpert.</p>\n<p>This page explains what custom software development in Gurugram looks like with us: the kinds of systems we build, how a project runs, how your data is protected, and what you get at the end.</p>\n\n<h2>Signs You Have Outgrown Off-the-Shelf Tools</h2>\n<ul class=\"check-list\">\n<li>Staff copy the same data between two or three tools every day.</li>\n<li>You pay for a SaaS product but use a small part of it, and the part you need is missing.</li>\n<li>Reports take someone a full day to put together at the end of each month.</li>\n<li>Only one person understands how the current spreadsheet works.</li>\n<li>Customers or vendors keep asking for status updates you cannot give quickly.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>If only one of these applies, a better-configured existing tool may be enough. If several apply, a custom system usually pays for itself in saved time and fewer errors.</p>\n\n<h2>What We Build</h2>\n<p>Most of our software projects fall into a few categories:</p>\n<ul class=\"tag-list\">\n<li>CRM and lead management</li>\n<li>ERP modules and inventory</li>\n<li>Booking and scheduling systems</li>\n<li>Customer and vendor portals</li>\n<li>Internal dashboards and reporting</li>\n<li>Field-force and dispatch tools</li>\n<li>SaaS products for startups</li>\n<li>API integrations between existing systems</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Typical examples: a broker portal for a developer selling projects along Dwarka Expressway, a patient-records and billing module for a multi-specialty clinic, or a subscription back office for a D2C brand that needs Razorpay, courier aggregator APIs and GST invoices in one place.</p>\n\n<h2>The Technology Underneath</h2>\n<p>We choose proven, widely used tools so that any competent developer can maintain your system later, including your own hires:</p>\n<ul class=\"check-list\">\n<li><strong>Backend:</strong> Laravel (PHP) or Node.js, with Python where data processing is involved.</li>\n<li><strong>Frontend:</strong> React or Vue for web dashboards and portals.</li>\n<li><strong>Database:</strong> MySQL or PostgreSQL, with Redis for caching and queues.</li>\n<li><strong>Hosting:</strong> AWS, DigitalOcean or your existing servers, with automated backups.</li>\n<li><strong>Integrations:</strong> UPI and card payments, WhatsApp Business API, SMS gateways, Tally or Zoho exports, Google Workspace.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>How a Project Runs</h2>\n<p>We split every project into phases, each with a clear output you can review:</p>\n<ol class=\"steps\">\n<li><strong>Discovery workshop (1–2 weeks).</strong> We sit with the people who will use the system, map the current process step by step, and list what must change. Our office is on Sohna Road in Sector 49, so teams from Udyog Vihar, MG Road or Golf Course Extension Road can come in for a working session, or we come to you.</li>\n<li><strong>Specification and prototype (1–2 weeks).</strong> A written scope, a data model and clickable screens. You sign off before development starts, and the fixed quote is based on this document.</li>\n<li><strong>Development in sprints (6–16 weeks).</strong> Two-week cycles, each ending with a demo on a staging server your team can log in to.</li>\n<li><strong>Data migration and user acceptance testing (2–3 weeks).</strong> We import your existing records, your team tests with real cases, and we fix what they find.</li>\n<li><strong>Go-live and training (1 week).</strong> Launch, hands-on training sessions and written guides for each user role.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>A small internal tool can be done in about two months. A multi-module system with several integrations can take four to six months. We would rather phase a large project than rush it.</p>\n\n<h2>Your Data and the DPDP Act</h2>\n<p>If your software stores customer or employee information, the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 applies to you as a data fiduciary. We build with that in mind: role-based access so staff see only what they need, audit logs of who changed what, encrypted connections, consent records where personal data is collected, and a practical way to find and delete a person\'s data on request. We also keep test and development environments free of real personal data.</p>\n\n<h2>Ownership, Handover and Support</h2>\n<p>You own everything we build for you once it is paid for: source code, database, documentation and designs. The code sits in a Git repository under your account from day one, not ours. At handover you get server credentials, a technical guide for future developers and an admin guide for your team. After a post-launch warranty period for bug fixes, you can choose a monthly support plan or take maintenance in-house.</p>\n\n<h2>How We Keep Quality Up</h2>\n<ul class=\"check-list\">\n<li>Peer code review on every change before it is merged.</li>\n<li>Automated tests for business rules such as pricing, commissions and tax calculations.</li>\n<li>A separate staging server that mirrors production.</li>\n<li>Security checks against common web risks such as SQL injection and broken access control.</li>\n<li>Load testing when the system will serve many users at once.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>Where Custom Software Projects Go Wrong</h2>\n<p>We see the same problems again and again when clients come to us after a failed attempt elsewhere. The biggest is skipping discovery and letting developers guess the process. The second is designing only for management reports and forgetting the staff who enter the data every day. Others include having no one on the client side who owns the project, leaving data migration to the last week, and accepting a system without documentation.</p>\n\n<h2>Who This Is Not For</h2>\n<p>Custom software is not the right choice if a standard tool like Zoho, Tally or a well-known CRM already covers most of what you need and your team is happy with it. It is also not a fit if you need a full system in three weeks, or if nobody in your business can give time to explain processes and test the software. In those cases we will point you to a simpler route.</p>\n\n<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>\n<h3>How do you price a custom software project?</h3>\n<p>Price depends on the number of modules and user roles, integrations, data migration and how complex your business rules are. We do not quote before understanding the process. After a free consultation and discovery, you get a fixed quote tied to a written scope.</p>\n<h3>Can the software connect with Tally or our existing tools?</h3>\n<p>Usually yes. Most tools offer an API or an import and export route. We check this during discovery and confirm what is possible before quoting.</p>\n<h3>Can we start with one module and add more later?</h3>\n<p>Yes, and we often recommend it. Starting with the module that removes the most manual work lets your team adapt before the next phase.</p>\n<h3>What if our developer leaves after handover?</h3>\n<p>Because we use common frameworks and hand over documentation and the full repository, any experienced Laravel, Node.js or React developer can pick up the code.</p>\n<h3>Do you work with companies outside Gurugram?</h3>\n<p>Yes. Our base is in Gurugram (many people still search for us as a Gurgaon agency), but discovery and reviews work well over video calls for clients elsewhere.</p>\n\n<p>If you are weighing custom software development in Gurugram, come and talk to us at Tower B1, Spaze I-Tech Park, Sohna Road, Sector 49, or call +91 9050126213. <a href=\"/contact-us\">Book a free consultation</a> and bring a sample of the spreadsheet or process you want to replace.</p>', meta_title='Custom Software Development Gurugram | TopWebExpert', meta_description='Replace spreadsheets with custom CRM, ERP, portals and dashboards built in Gurugram. DPDP-aware, full source code handover, fixed quote after discovery.', meta_keywords='custom software development gurugram, software development company gurgaon, crm development gurugram, erp software development india, web application development gurugram', updated_at=NOW(), tier=1 WHERE service_slug='software-development' AND location_id=(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE slug='gurgaon' LIMIT 1);
UPDATE city_pages SET title='UI/UX Design', content='<p>Good UI/UX design is less about how a screen looks and more about whether a person can finish what they came to do without thinking about it. A buyer comparing apartments on Golf Course Extension Road should find the floor plan and price-on-request button in seconds. A clinic patient should book a slot without calling anyone. A finance manager in a GCC office should read a dashboard without a training session. At TopWebExpert, UI/UX design is a stage of its own, done before development, and it is where we catch most of the problems that would be expensive to fix in code.</p>\n\n<h2>What You Receive at the End</h2>\n<p>Clients often ask what they are actually paying for, so we start with the deliverables. A full UI/UX engagement typically produces:</p>\n<ul class=\"check-list\">\n<li><strong>Research summary:</strong> findings from user interviews, analytics review and a look at how competitors handle the same tasks.</li>\n<li><strong>User flows:</strong> diagrams of each key journey, such as signing up, searching, booking or paying.</li>\n<li><strong>Wireframes:</strong> low-detail layouts of every screen, agreed before visual design starts.</li>\n<li><strong>High-fidelity designs in Figma:</strong> final screens for mobile and desktop, including empty, loading and error states.</li>\n<li><strong>Clickable prototype:</strong> a link you can open on your phone and share with your team or investors.</li>\n<li><strong>Design system:</strong> colours, type, spacing, buttons, form fields and components, documented so developers build consistently.</li>\n<li><strong>Developer handover:</strong> annotated specs, exported assets and a walkthrough call with whoever will build it.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>For smaller projects, such as redesigning a single checkout or onboarding flow, we scope down to the pieces that matter.</p>\n\n<h2>How We Research Your Users</h2>\n<p>We talk to real users, not just stakeholders. For a B2B SaaS product that might mean five or six interviews with customers over video. For a consumer app it can mean sitting with users at your store or clinic and watching them try the current flow. We pay attention to local habits that change design decisions:</p>\n<ul class=\"check-list\">\n<li>Many users switch between Hindi and English, so labels need to be short and clear in both.</li>\n<li>A large share of traffic comes from budget Android phones with smaller screens, so tap targets and text size matter.</li>\n<li>People expect to pay through UPI and to get updates on WhatsApp, and flows should match that.</li>\n<li>OTP login is familiar; long passwords and email verification loops cause drop-offs.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>The Design Process and Timeline</h2>\n<ol class=\"steps\">\n<li><strong>Week 1: Kickoff and audit.</strong> A workshop at our Sohna Road office in Sector 49 or at your premises, review of analytics and the existing product, and agreement on the key user tasks.</li>\n<li><strong>Weeks 2–3: Research and flows.</strong> Interviews, competitor review and user flow diagrams.</li>\n<li><strong>Weeks 3–5: Wireframes and testing.</strong> Low-fidelity screens, tested with a handful of users to find confusion early.</li>\n<li><strong>Weeks 5–8: Visual design.</strong> High-fidelity screens and the clickable prototype, with two structured review rounds.</li>\n<li><strong>Weeks 8–9: Design system and handover.</strong> Component library, specs and a handover session with the development team.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>A focused redesign of one flow can take three to four weeks. A new product with many user roles may take longer than nine.</p>\n\n<h2>Tools We Work With</h2>\n<ul class=\"tag-list\">\n<li>Figma</li>\n<li>FigJam</li>\n<li>Maze</li>\n<li>Google Analytics 4</li>\n<li>Microsoft Clarity</li>\n<li>Hotjar</li>\n<li>Google Forms for surveys</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>Accessibility Is Part of the Brief</h2>\n<p>We design to WCAG 2.1 AA as a baseline: sufficient colour contrast, readable font sizes, visible focus states, labelled form fields and layouts that work when users enlarge text. This helps older users and people with low vision, and it also makes screens easier to use in bright sunlight on a phone, which matters for field staff and delivery users.</p>\n\n<h2>How We Check the Design Before It Is Built</h2>\n<p>Every design goes through usability testing with real users, even if only five people, because that is usually enough to show the biggest problems. We also run a heuristic review against established usability principles, check every screen for missing states, and confirm with your developers that each component is practical to build in your chosen framework. It is far cheaper to move a button in Figma than in production code.</p>\n\n<h2>Ownership of the Design Files</h2>\n<p>You own the final designs, the Figma files and the design system after payment. We transfer the files to your Figma workspace, so your team or any future agency can keep working from them. Fonts and stock images are licensed in your name where needed.</p>\n\n<h2>Common UX Mistakes</h2>\n<ul class=\"check-list\">\n<li>Designing for the founder\'s taste rather than the user\'s task.</li>\n<li>Starting visual design before the flows are agreed, which leads to repeated rework.</li>\n<li>Forgetting error, empty and offline states, so developers invent them on the fly.</li>\n<li>Asking for too much information at sign-up.</li>\n<li>Handing developers static images with no specs or component library.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>When This Service Is Not the Right Fit</h2>\n<p>If you only need a few banners or a quick visual refresh of an existing website, a full UX process is more than you need; a graphic design task will do. It is also not a fit if the product decisions are already locked and there is no room to change flows based on what users tell us, or if there is no time for your team to review designs.</p>\n\n<h2>FAQs About UI/UX Design</h2>\n<h3>What is the difference between UI and UX?</h3>\n<p>UX is how the product works: the steps, the order of information and how easy it is to finish a task. UI is how it looks: layout, colour, type and components. We do both, and UX comes first.</p>\n<h3>How is the cost worked out?</h3>\n<p>It depends on the number of screens and user roles, how much research is needed, and whether you need a full design system. After a free consultation we send a fixed quote based on an agreed scope.</p>\n<h3>Can you redesign our existing app without rebuilding it?</h3>\n<p>Often, yes. We can work within your current framework and design system, and prioritise changes that improve the most-used flows first.</p>\n<h3>Can our in-house developers build from your designs?</h3>\n<p>Yes. Our handover includes specs, assets and a walkthrough, and we stay available for questions during development.</p>\n<h3>Do you only work with companies in Gurugram?</h3>\n<p>No, but being local helps with in-person research. Clients from Cyber City, Sector 29 or anywhere in Gurgaon can join workshops at our office easily.</p>\n\n<p>If you are planning UI/UX design in Gurugram for a new product or a redesign, visit us at Tower B1, Spaze I-Tech Park, Sohna Road, Sector 49, or call +91 9050126213. <a href=\"/contact-us\">Book a free consultation</a> and show us the flow that frustrates your users most.</p>', meta_title='UI/UX Design Services in Gurugram | TopWebExpert', meta_description='User research, wireframes, Figma prototypes and design systems for apps and websites, tested with real users. Sector 49 Gurugram studio. Free consultation.', meta_keywords='ui ux design gurugram, ui ux design company gurgaon, figma prototype design, app ui design services, website ux design gurugram', updated_at=NOW(), tier=1 WHERE service_slug='ui-ux-design' AND location_id=(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE slug='gurgaon' LIMIT 1);
UPDATE city_pages SET title='Website Designing & Development in Gurugram', content='<p>For most Gurugram businesses, the website is the second thing a prospect checks after hearing your name. A buyer in a Cyber City office, a family checking a clinic on Sohna Road, a channel partner looking at a Dwarka Expressway project: most open your site on a phone, often on patchy mobile data, and decide quickly whether to call. We are a design and development team based in Sector 49, working with local businesses for 7+ years. This page explains how we plan, build and hand over a website, what we need from you, and where we are honestly not the right choice.</p><h2>What a finished website from us includes</h2><p>Every project is scoped separately, but a typical business website leaves our hands with these things in place:</p><ul class=\"check-list\"><li><strong>Designs you have approved</strong> for both mobile and desktop before any code is written, so nothing surprises you at launch.</li><li><strong>A responsive front end</strong> in clean HTML, CSS and JavaScript, or a WordPress theme built around your content rather than a heavy multipurpose theme.</li><li><strong>Enquiry paths that match how people here contact a business</strong>: tap-to-call, a WhatsApp chat button, and a short form that emails your team and keeps a copy of every lead.</li><li><strong>On-page SEO groundwork</strong>: unique page titles and descriptions, a clean heading structure, an XML sitemap, business schema markup and a link to your Google Business Profile.</li><li><strong>SSL, spam protection on forms and a backup routine</strong> set up on your hosting.</li><li><strong>Google Analytics and Search Console</strong> connected and verified under your company\'s own Google account.</li></ul><h2>Custom code or WordPress?</h2><p>This is the first decision we help you make. The right answer depends on how often the site will change and who will change it.</p><h3>Custom-coded site</h3><p>Suits a company profile, a product landing page or a site with one specific tool, such as a quote request form with part-number lookup for an auto-parts supplier in the Manesar belt. It loads fast and has very little to patch, but text changes usually need a developer.</p><h3>WordPress</h3><p>Suits teams that will publish updates themselves: blog posts, new project pages for a real estate developer, or doctor profiles for a hospital. It needs regular updates and a short, sensible plugin list to stay fast and secure.</p><h2>How a project runs, week by week</h2><p>A business website of 8 to 15 pages usually takes <strong>4 to 7 weeks</strong> from sign-off to launch. Most delays come from content, not code.</p><ol class=\"steps\"><li><strong>Week 1, discovery.</strong> We meet at our Sohna Road office, at yours or on a video call, list your services and audiences, look at competitor sites and agree a sitemap.</li><li><strong>Week 2, wireframes and design.</strong> You see the home page and one inner page in mobile and desktop layouts, and we revise until you approve.</li><li><strong>Weeks 3 to 5, development.</strong> We build on a private staging link you can open at any time, adding your content as it arrives.</li><li><strong>Week 6, testing.</strong> Speed, forms, browsers, devices and SEO checks, described below.</li><li><strong>Launch.</strong> We move the site to your live domain, set up 301 redirects from any old URLs so you keep the search traffic they earned, and watch Search Console for errors in the following weeks.</li></ol><h2>What we need from you</h2><p>How quickly you can provide these is the biggest factor in whether we hit the timeline:</p><ul class=\"check-list\"><li>Your logo in vector or high-resolution format, and brand colours if you have them.</li><li>Text for each service, or an hour with someone senior so we can draft it for you.</li><li>Real photos of your team, office, products or finished work.</li><li>Logins for your domain registrar and hosting, or approval for us to set up hosting in your company\'s name.</li><li>One person on your side who can approve designs and copy within a few working days.</li></ul><h2>How we test before launch</h2><p>A site does not go live until it passes these checks on a real mid-range Android phone as well as on desktop:</p><ul class=\"check-list\"><li><strong>Core Web Vitals.</strong> We measure LCP, INP and CLS in PageSpeed Insights and fix what slows the page down, usually oversized images, render-blocking scripts or too many web fonts.</li><li><strong>Slow network test.</strong> We throttle the connection to see how the site behaves on weak mobile data, not just office Wi-Fi.</li><li><strong>Enquiry tests.</strong> Every form, call link and WhatsApp button is tested so we know each lead actually reaches you.</li><li><strong>Security basics.</strong> HTTPS on every page, security headers, no leftover test files or exposed admin paths, and strong unique passwords.</li><li><strong>Backup and restore.</strong> We take a full backup and confirm it can actually be restored.</li></ul><h2>Mistakes we often fix on local business websites</h2><ul class=\"check-list\"><li>The phone number shown as an image, so mobile visitors cannot tap to call.</li><li>A large homepage slider that pushes the real offer below the fold and slows every visit.</li><li>The domain registered in a former employee\'s or freelancer\'s personal account, so the business cannot renew or move it.</li><li>Generic copy that could belong to any company, with no mention of the services, areas or industries you actually serve.</li></ul><h2>Who this service is not for</h2><p>We are not a good fit if you need a site live in three days, want hundreds of near-identical pages made for search engines rather than people, or expect a website alone to bring leads without any work on content or marketing. If you only need a basic one-page presence, a site builder such as Wix may serve you better than an agency.</p><h2>What decides the cost</h2><p>We do not publish a price list, because two \"10-page websites\" can differ a lot in effort. The main cost drivers are the number of unique page layouts, whether we write the content, custom features such as booking, calculators or a client login, integration with a CRM or ERP, and extra languages such as Hindi. After a free consultation you get a fixed quote with the scope written out, not an open-ended hourly bill.</p><h2>Ownership after handover</h2><p>The domain, hosting, website files and Google accounts stay in your company\'s name. At handover you receive every login, the source files, and a short walkthrough on editing content. Any support period after launch is written into the quote so both sides know what is covered.</p><h2>Questions Gurugram business owners ask us</h2><h3>Do I have to visit your office?</h3><p>No. Many clients meet us once at Spaze I-Tech Park and handle the rest on calls and WhatsApp. For offices in Cyber City, Udyog Vihar or on Golf Course Road, we can come to you.</p><h3>Can you redesign my current site without losing Google rankings?</h3><p>Yes, with planning. We crawl the old site, map every URL to its new page, add 301 redirects and keep the content that already ranks. Rankings can shift for a few weeks after any redesign, so we watch Search Console closely.</p><h3>Will you write the content for us?</h3><p>We can. We interview you or your team and draft pages in plain English for your approval. Good content still needs your knowledge of customers and process, so expect to spend a few hours with us on it.</p><h3>Who owns the website once it is live?</h3><p>You do. Everything is registered to your company, and you can move the site to another developer or host at any time without asking us.</p><h3>Do we have to take hosting and maintenance from you?</h3><p>No. We can set up hosting in your name and offer a maintenance plan, but your in-house team can manage the site instead if you prefer.</p><p>Whether you still say Gurgaon or have switched to Gurugram, our office is easy to reach: Tower B1, Spaze I-Tech Park, Sohna Road, Sector 49. <a href=\"/contact-us\">Book a free consultation</a> or call +91 9050126213, and we will review your current site and goals and give you a realistic timeline before any quote.</p>', meta_title='Website Design & Development in Gurugram | TopWebExpert', meta_description='Website design and development from our Sohna Road office: mobile-first builds, WhatsApp enquiries, Core Web Vitals testing and full ownership handed to you.', meta_keywords='website design company gurugram, web development company in gurgaon, website designing gurugram, business website development gurgaon, website redesign gurugram', updated_at=NOW(), tier=1 WHERE service_slug='web-development-company' AND location_id=(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE slug='gurgaon' LIMIT 1);
UPDATE city_pages SET title='Website Maintenance Services in Gurugram', content='<p>A website is not finished at launch. Plugins release security fixes, PHP versions reach end of life, SSL certificates need renewing, forms stop sending email after a hosting change, and pages slowly get heavier as new images are added. None of this is visible until something breaks, often at the worst time: during a property launch, an admissions season or a sale. We look after business websites for Gurugram companies from our Sohna Road office, and this page explains what regular maintenance involves and whether you need it.</p><h2>Signs your website needs attention now</h2><ul class=\"check-list\"><li>Your WordPress dashboard shows a long list of pending updates.</li><li>Enquiries have dropped, and nobody has checked whether the contact form still works.</li><li>The site takes several seconds to load on a phone.</li><li>Google Search Console reports errors, or you have never set it up.</li><li>You do not know when the last backup was taken, or where it is stored.</li><li>Your browser shows a \"Not secure\" warning, or the SSL certificate expired once before.</li><li>The person who built the site has moved on and nobody has the logins.</li></ul><h2>What a maintenance plan covers</h2><p>The exact list depends on your platform, but a typical plan follows this routine.</p><h3>Every week</h3><ul class=\"check-list\"><li>Core, theme and plugin updates, tested on a staging copy first for sites that take payments or bookings.</li><li>Malware and file-change scans.</li><li>Uptime monitoring, with alerts to us if the site goes down.</li><li>Test submission of your main enquiry form.</li></ul><h3>Every month</h3><ul class=\"check-list\"><li>Backup check: confirm daily off-site backups are running, and do a test restore to staging from time to time.</li><li>PageSpeed and Core Web Vitals check on key pages, with fixes for new problems such as oversized images.</li><li>Broken link and 404 error review in Search Console.</li><li>Small content changes within the plan\'s allowance: updating prices, team members, timings or banners.</li><li>A short plain-English report of what was done and anything that needs a decision from you.</li></ul><h3>Every quarter</h3><ul class=\"check-list\"><li>Review of user accounts, removing ex-employees and agencies who no longer need access.</li><li>PHP version and hosting health check, including disk space and email deliverability.</li><li>Domain and SSL renewal dates confirmed, so nothing lapses.</li><li>Plugin and app review, removing anything unused.</li></ul><h2>Platforms we maintain</h2><ul class=\"tag-list\"><li>WordPress</li><li>WooCommerce</li><li>Shopify</li><li>Custom PHP sites</li><li>Static HTML sites</li><li>cPanel and Hostinger hosting</li><li>VPS and cloud servers</li></ul><p>Shopify stores need less technical upkeep because Shopify handles hosting and security, so maintenance there focuses on apps, theme updates, speed and content.</p><h2>The first month: a health audit</h2><p>We do not take over a site blind. Every plan begins with an audit that usually takes one to two weeks:</p><ol class=\"steps\"><li><strong>Access and ownership check.</strong> We confirm the domain, hosting and Google accounts are in your company\'s name, and help recover any that are not.</li><li><strong>Full backup</strong> taken before we touch anything.</li><li><strong>Security scan</strong> for malware, outdated software, unknown admin users and nulled plugins.</li><li><strong>Speed and SEO baseline</strong> recorded, so later reports compare against real starting numbers.</li><li><strong>Fix list</strong> shared with you, separating urgent problems from things that can wait.</li></ol><h2>Access we need from you</h2><p>An administrator login for the website, hosting control panel access (or a hosting account where we can be added as a user), DNS access at your domain registrar, and Search Console and Analytics access for your Google account. We use a password manager, and all access is returned or removed if you end the plan.</p><h2>What is not part of routine maintenance</h2><p>New pages beyond the plan\'s allowance, redesigns, new features, integrations and large content projects are quoted separately. So is cleaning a site that was already hacked before the plan started, because that work varies a lot. We tell you before any extra work begins, never after.</p><h2>If your site is hacked or down today</h2><p>We first take a copy of the infected site for investigation, then restore a clean backup if one exists, or clean the files and database by hand if not. We then find how the attacker got in, change every password, remove the weakness, and request a review in Google Search Console if Google flagged the site. After that, regular maintenance is what keeps it from happening again.</p><h2>When a maintenance plan is not worth it</h2><p>If you have a static site that rarely changes, an in-house developer who already handles updates, or a Shopify store your team manages comfortably, a monthly plan may not add much. A yearly check-up may be enough, and we are happy to say so.</p><h2>How plans are priced</h2><p>Cost depends on the platform, the number of plugins or apps, whether the site takes payments, how much content work you need each month, and the response time you want. We quote a fixed monthly or annual fee after a free consultation and an initial look at your site.</p><h2>Maintenance FAQs</h2><h3>Can you maintain a site that another agency built?</h3><p>Yes. Most sites we maintain were built by someone else. The first-month audit is how we learn the site and find any hidden problems.</p><h3>Will updates break my website?</h3><p>They can, which is why we test updates on a staging copy for important sites and always take a backup first. If something still breaks, we roll back and fix it.</p><h3>How quickly do you respond if the site goes down?</h3><p>Response times are written into your plan. Uptime monitoring alerts us directly, so we often know before you do.</p><h3>Do you also handle hosting renewals and business email?</h3><p>We track renewal dates and can manage hosting for you, but the accounts stay in your company\'s name and billing stays with you.</p><h3>Can we cancel the plan?</h3><p>Yes. On cancellation we hand over all logins, the latest backups and a note on the site\'s current state.</p><p>Many of the sites we look after were built years ago, some still listing an old Gurgaon address. Wherever yours stands, meet us at Tower B1, Spaze I-Tech Park, Sohna Road, Sector 49, or <a href=\"/contact-us\">book a free consultation</a> and share your site link. We will point out the most urgent issues before you decide on anything.</p>', meta_title='Website Maintenance Services Gurugram | TopWebExpert', meta_description='Weekly updates, malware scans, tested backups, uptime alerts and speed checks for WordPress, WooCommerce, Shopify and PHP sites, from our Sohna Road office.', meta_keywords='website maintenance services gurugram, website maintenance company in gurgaon, wordpress maintenance gurugram, hacked website repair gurgaon, website support services gurugram', updated_at=NOW(), tier=1 WHERE service_slug='website-maintenance-services' AND location_id=(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE slug='gurgaon' LIMIT 1);
UPDATE city_pages SET title='WhatsApp Marketing', content='<p>Most businesses in Gurugram already use WhatsApp every day. A clinic on Sohna Road confirms appointments on it, a coaching centre sends batch timings, and a showroom on MG Road shares product photos with walk-in customers. The problem is that most of this runs from one staff phone on the regular WhatsApp Business app. Chats get lost when that person is on leave, and broadcasts only reach people who saved your number.</p>\n<p>Our WhatsApp marketing work moves you from that setup to the official <strong>WhatsApp Business Platform</strong> (often called the WhatsApp API). We are TopWebExpert, based in Sector 49 on Sohna Road, and this page explains what the service involves, what it needs from you, and when it is not worth doing.</p>\n\n<h2>App vs. API: which one do you actually need?</h2>\n<p>Not every business needs the API. The free WhatsApp Business app is fine if you handle a few dozen chats a day and one or two people reply to them. The platform makes sense when any of these is true:</p>\n<ul class=\"check-list\">\n<li>More than one person needs to reply from the same business number, such as a sales team or front desk staff working in shifts.</li>\n<li>You want to send updates to hundreds or thousands of customers who have opted in, not just to people who saved your contact.</li>\n<li>Leads from your website, Google Ads or Meta ads should get an instant WhatsApp reply, and should be logged in your CRM.</li>\n<li>You need order, booking or payment reminders to go out automatically.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>If none of these apply yet, we will tell you to stay on the app and set it up well (catalogue, quick replies, labels, away messages). That takes an afternoon.</p>\n\n<h2>How the setup works, step by step</h2>\n<p>A typical setup takes one to three weeks. Most of it is waiting on verification and template approvals.</p>\n<ol class=\"steps\">\n<li><strong>Number decision.</strong> We check whether your chosen number is already on the WhatsApp app and what your provider supports. Some businesses move the number fully to the platform; others take a fresh number for it.</li>\n<li><strong>Meta Business verification.</strong> Your business is verified in Meta Business Manager using documents such as GST registration or a certificate of incorporation, and a website on a matching domain. Mismatched details are the usual cause of delays.</li>\n<li><strong>Provider and inbox.</strong> You connect either directly through Meta\'s Cloud API or through a Business Solution Provider that adds a shared team inbox, chatbot builder and campaign tools. We compare options against your volume and budget.</li>\n<li><strong>Display name.</strong> Meta reviews your display name, which should match your brand on your website and signage.</li>\n<li><strong>Opt-in collection.</strong> We add clear opt-in points: a checkbox on website forms, a line on Meta lead forms, a QR code at your reception or store counter, and a click-to-WhatsApp button on ads.</li>\n<li><strong>Template writing and approval.</strong> Every message you start (outside a customer\'s 24-hour reply window) must use a template approved by Meta. We write and submit these, usually a first batch of five to ten.</li>\n<li><strong>Automation and CRM link.</strong> Welcome replies, FAQ menus, and routing to the right team member are built, and new chats are pushed to your CRM or a Google Sheet.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h2>Rules that decide whether your number survives</h2>\n<p>WhatsApp numbers get restricted or blocked when too many recipients block or report them. Meta tracks this as a quality rating, and a low rating limits how many people you can message per day. These rules protect that rating:</p>\n<ul class=\"check-list\">\n<li><strong>Only message people who opted in.</strong> Blasting a purchased list of Gurugram phone numbers is the fastest way to lose a number, and we don\'t do it.</li>\n<li><strong>Use the right template category.</strong> Meta classifies templates as marketing, utility or authentication, and charges differently for each. An order update can be utility; an offer is marketing. Mislabelled templates get re-categorised or rejected.</li>\n<li><strong>Respect the 24-hour window.</strong> When a customer messages you, you can reply freely for 24 hours. After that, only templates can be sent.</li>\n<li><strong>Give an easy way out.</strong> Every marketing template includes a simple opt-out, and opt-outs are honoured immediately.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Meta sets message charges by category and country and revises them from time to time, so we always check the current rate card before planning a campaign budget. These charges are paid to Meta or your provider, separately from our fee.</p>\n\n<h2>What happens every month</h2>\n<ul class=\"check-list\">\n<li>Planning two to four broadcast campaigns with you, based on what you actually have to say: new stock, a seasonal offer, a site visit weekend, a webinar.</li>\n<li>Splitting your contact list by interest or stage (new enquiry, past customer, inactive) so each group gets relevant messages.</li>\n<li>Writing and getting approval for new templates as needed.</li>\n<li>Checking chatbot conversations for questions it fails to answer and fixing the flows.</li>\n<li>Watching the quality rating and pausing any campaign that triggers a spike in blocks.</li>\n<li>A monthly report and a short call to decide what to change.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>What we need from you</h2>\n<p>We need business documents for verification, a person who owns the Meta Business Manager account (it should stay in your name, not ours), agreed answers to your common customer questions, and someone on your team who will reply to chats that the bot hands over. That matters most: if a hot lead writes back at 11 am and nobody answers until evening, the automation has not helped.</p>\n\n<h2>How we judge whether it is working</h2>\n<p>We report on numbers that come straight from the platform and your CRM, not vanity counts:</p>\n<ul class=\"tag-list\">\n<li>Delivery rate</li>\n<li>Read rate</li>\n<li>Reply rate</li>\n<li>Block and opt-out rate</li>\n<li>First response time</li>\n<li>Leads or bookings per campaign</li>\n<li>Cost per conversation or lead</li>\n</ul>\n<p>A campaign with a high read rate but no replies usually means the message had no clear next step. A rising block rate means the audience or frequency is wrong.</p>\n\n<h2>When WhatsApp is the wrong channel</h2>\n<p>WhatsApp marketing is not a good fit if you have no opted-in customers and no plan to collect them, if nobody on your team can answer chats during working hours, or if your product needs long, formal documentation that suits email better. It also suits nobody who wants to send the same promotion to everyone every few days; that annoys recipients and damages the number.</p>\n\n<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>\n<h3>Can I keep using my existing WhatsApp number?</h3>\n<p>Usually yes. Depending on your provider, the number is either moved to the platform or, where Meta supports it, used on both the Business app and the platform. We confirm the options, including what happens to chat history, before anything is changed.</p>\n<h3>Is sending bulk WhatsApp messages legal?</h3>\n<p>Sending to people who have agreed to hear from you, through the official platform with approved templates, is how WhatsApp is meant to be used for business. Unofficial bulk-sending software breaks WhatsApp\'s terms, and numbers used that way often get banned.</p>\n<h3>How much does it cost?</h3>\n<p>There are three parts: Meta\'s per-message charges, any provider or inbox subscription, and our setup and management fee. Our fee depends on how many templates, flows and integrations you need and how many campaigns run each month. We give a fixed quote after a free consultation.</p>\n<h3>Can the chatbot answer in Hindi?</h3>\n<p>Yes. Templates and bot replies can be written in Hindi, English or both. Many customers in Gurgaon write in Hinglish, so we keep the language simple.</p>\n<h3>How soon can we send our first campaign?</h3>\n<p>If your business documents are in order, the first approved templates and a small campaign to existing opted-in customers can usually go out within two to three weeks of starting.</p>\n\n<p>If you want to see whether the WhatsApp Business Platform is worth it for your business, visit us at our office in Spaze I-Tech Park on Sohna Road, Sector 49, or call +91 9050126213. <a href=\"/contact-us\">Book a free consultation</a> and we will review your current setup</p>', meta_title='WhatsApp Marketing in Gurugram | TopWebExpert', meta_description='WhatsApp Business Platform setup in Gurugram: Meta verification, approved templates, opt-in collection, CRM-linked chatbots and monthly campaign management.', meta_keywords='whatsapp marketing gurugram, whatsapp business api gurgaon, whatsapp marketing agency gurgaon, bulk whatsapp messages gurgaon, whatsapp chatbot for business', updated_at=NOW(), tier=1 WHERE service_slug='whatsapp-marketing' AND location_id=(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE slug='gurgaon' LIMIT 1);
UPDATE city_pages SET title='WordPress Development in Gurugram', content='<p>WordPress powers a large share of business websites, including many in Gurugram, and it is a good choice when your own team wants to add pages, publish news or update listings without calling a developer. It also has a reputation for being slow and getting hacked. Both problems usually come from how a site was built and looked after, not from WordPress itself. We build, repair and look after WordPress sites from our office on Sohna Road, and this page explains our approach.</p><h2>Three situations we are usually called in for</h2><h3>1. You need a new WordPress site</h3><p>A company that wants its marketing team to publish case notes, a real estate developer adding new projects and construction updates, a coaching institute posting batch schedules and results announcements, a hospital maintaining doctor profiles. In each case the structure of the content matters more than the look, so we plan content types first and design around them.</p><h3>2. Your current site is slow, broken or hacked</h3><p>Typical symptoms: the admin panel takes ages to load, a plugin update broke the layout, Google shows a \"This site may be hacked\" warning, or strange Japanese or pharma pages appear in search results under your domain. We diagnose the cause, clean it up, and fix what allowed it to happen.</p><h3>3. You are moving to, or away from, WordPress</h3><p>We migrate sites from custom PHP, Wix or older CMS platforms into WordPress, and occasionally advise moving off WordPress when it no longer fits. Either way, every old URL gets a 301 redirect so search traffic is not lost.</p><h2>How we build: a theme made for your content, and few plugins</h2><p>Most slow WordPress sites run a multipurpose theme loaded with demo features, a heavy page builder and dozens of plugins. We work the other way round. We build a lightweight custom theme, or a child theme of a well-maintained base theme, and use the native block editor (Gutenberg) with custom blocks for your repeating sections. For structured content such as property listings, courses or doctor profiles, we create custom post types with fields your team fills in, so layouts stay consistent and nobody has to wrestle with design tools. If your team is already comfortable with Elementor and wants to keep it, we can work with it, but we will explain the speed trade-off first.</p><h2>Our usual toolkit</h2><ul class=\"tag-list\"><li>Gutenberg block editor</li><li>Custom post types</li><li>Advanced Custom Fields</li><li>Rank Math or Yoast SEO</li><li>LiteSpeed Cache or WP Rocket</li><li>Wordfence</li><li>UpdraftPlus backups</li><li>WooCommerce, when you sell online</li></ul><p>Every plugin must justify its place. Before adding one, we check its update history and whether a few lines of theme code would do the same job.</p><h2>Speed and security baseline for every site</h2><ul class=\"check-list\"><li><strong>Core Web Vitals</strong> checked on mobile in PageSpeed Insights, with images served in WebP, lazy loading below the fold and unused scripts removed from pages that do not need them.</li><li><strong>Page caching</strong> matched to your host, for example LiteSpeed Cache on LiteSpeed servers.</li><li><strong>Login protection</strong>: no \"admin\" username, strong passwords, limited login attempts and two-factor authentication for administrators.</li><li><strong>Least privilege</strong>: content writers get Editor or Author roles, not Administrator.</li><li><strong>File editing disabled</strong> in the dashboard, XML-RPC turned off if nothing needs it, and PHP kept on a supported version.</li><li><strong>Daily off-site backups</strong> with a restore tested before handover.</li></ul><h2>A typical WordPress project timeline</h2><ol class=\"steps\"><li><strong>Content planning</strong> (week 1): sitemap, content types, which fields each one needs and who will edit what.</li><li><strong>Design</strong> (weeks 1 to 2): key templates for mobile and desktop, approved by you.</li><li><strong>Theme and block development</strong> (weeks 2 to 4) on a staging site you can log into.</li><li><strong>Content entry and training</strong> (weeks 4 to 5): we load the first set of content and show your team how to add more.</li><li><strong>Launch and checks</strong> (week 5 or 6): redirects, Search Console, backups and a final speed test on the live server.</li></ol><p>A 10 to 20 page site usually takes 4 to 6 weeks. A repair job on a hacked or slow site is normally a matter of days once we have access.</p><h2>What you give us, and what we hand back</h2><p>We need your content and images, access to hosting and the domain\'s DNS, and for existing sites an administrator login plus any premium plugin licence keys. At handover you receive administrator access in your own name, the theme source code, a list of every plugin with its purpose, licences registered to your email, and a short recorded training session your staff can rewatch. You own all of it, and you can move to another developer whenever you like.</p><h2>Where WordPress sites go wrong</h2><ul class=\"check-list\"><li><strong>Nulled themes and plugins.</strong> Pirated copies of paid themes are a common source of malware. We replace them with licensed versions or free alternatives.</li><li><strong>Updates ignored for months</strong>, then run all at once on the live site, which breaks things.</li><li><strong>No staging copy</strong>, so every experiment happens in front of customers.</li><li><strong>A single administrator account</strong> held by a freelancer who is no longer reachable.</li><li><strong>Cheap shared hosting</strong> on an old PHP version, which no amount of caching can fully fix.</li></ul><h2>When we would advise against WordPress</h2><p>If your site will have five pages that change once a year, a static site is cheaper to run and has almost nothing to update. If you are building a web application with user dashboards, complex permissions or heavy transactions, a framework such as Laravel is usually a better base. And if nobody on your team will ever log in, most of WordPress\'s advantage disappears. We would rather tell you this at the start than build the wrong thing.</p><h2>Cost and quotes</h2><p>The quote depends on the number of templates and content types, custom functionality, the amount of content we enter, and for repair jobs, the state of the existing site. We give a fixed quote after a free consultation, and for an existing site, after a quick audit.</p><h2>Common questions about WordPress</h2><h3>Is WordPress secure enough for a business site?</h3><p>Yes, when it is kept updated, uses licensed and maintained plugins, and has proper login protection and backups. Most hacked WordPress sites we see missed one of those basics.</p><h3>Can my team really update the site without a developer?</h3><p>For everyday content, yes. We build editing screens around your content, so adding a new project, doctor or course is a matter of filling in fields. Layout changes and new features still need a developer.</p><h3>Our site was built on Elementor. Do we have to rebuild it?</h3><p>Not necessarily. We first try to speed it up and clean it. If the page builder is the main bottleneck, we will show you the test results and let you decide whether a rebuild is worth it.</p><h3>Can you fix a site another agency built?</h3><p>Yes. We start with an audit of the theme, plugins, hosting and security, then tell you what needs fixing and what can stay.</p><h3>How often does a WordPress site need updates?</h3><p>Plugin and core updates come out regularly, so we recommend checking at least weekly, with updates tested on staging first for any site that takes payments or bookings.</p><p>If you have a WordPress site in Gurugram that needs building, rescuing or migrating, including older sites still showing a Gurgaon address in the footer, come and see us at Tower B1, Spaze I-Tech Park, Sohna Road, Sector 49. <a href=\"/contact-us\">Book a free consultation</a> and share your current site link; we will look at it before we meet.</p>', meta_title='WordPress Development in Gurugram | TopWebExpert', meta_description='New WordPress builds, hacked or slow site repair and migrations from our Sohna Road office. Lightweight themes, few plugins, tested backups and full handover.', meta_keywords='wordpress development gurugram, wordpress developer in gurgaon, wordpress website design gurugram, hacked wordpress site repair gurgaon, wordpress speed optimization gurugram', updated_at=NOW(), tier=1 WHERE service_slug='wordpress-development' AND location_id=(SELECT id FROM locations WHERE slug='gurgaon' LIMIT 1);
